    ",{\"vid\":\"dngqR9gcDDw\",\"title\":\"Free To Choose 1980 - Vol. 01 The Power of the Market - Full Video\",\"channel\":\"Free To Choose Network\",\"summary\":\"The first episode of Milton Friedman's 1980 Free To Choose series, on how markets and voluntary exchange organize economic activity and the price system. It includes visits to Hong Kong, the U.S. and Scotland and a panel discussion with critics.\",\"why_hn\":\"Commenters say it made market economics click for them and find it an interesting documentary relevant to welfare and UBI debates.\",\"content_type\":\"documentary\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"free market economics\",\"categories\":[\"Microeconomics & behavioral economics\",\"Macroeconomics & financial crises\"],\"tags\":[\"milton friedman\",\"free markets\",\"price system\",\"economics\",\"1980s\"],\"quote\":\"What really made it click was Milton Friedman's\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.5},{\"vid\":\"dw_mRaIHb-M\",\"title\":\"Aamer Rahman (Fear of a Brown Planet) - Reverse Racism\",\"channel\":\"FEAR OF A BROWN PLANET\",\"summary\":\"Aamer Rahman of Fear of a Brown Planet delivers a stand-up routine on so-called reverse racism, arguing about power imbalance and why criticism of a dominant group is not equivalent to racism.\",\"why_hn\":\"Pointed to as a comedic but clear explanation of power dynamics in discussions of race and diversity in tech.\",\"content_type\":\"comedy\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"racism and power\",\"categories\":[\"Stand-up & sketch comedy\",\"Social issues & culture\"],\"tags\":[\"stand-up\",\"aamer rahman\",\"reverse racism\",\"race\",\"social commentary\"],\"quote\":\"the very best explanation is long-form stand-up comedy. If you don't understand, you really should watch this.\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":2.5},{\"vid\":\"eBCbdThIJNE\",\"title\":\"Power Satellites & Space Based Solar Power\",\"channel\":\"Isaac Arthur\",\"summary\":\"Isaac Arthur explores space-based solar power, in which satellites beam energy down via microwaves to rectennas on Earth. He discusses feasibility, profitability and its role in spurring space colonization.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN commenters recommend it as the best overview of power satellites, with pros and cons beyond the construction cost.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"space-based solar power\",\"categories\":[\"Renewables, batteries & storage\",\"Space exploration & spaceflight\"],\"tags\":[\"power satellites\",\"solar power\",\"microwave transmission\",\"rectenna\",\"space energy\"],\"quote\":\"Issac Arthur usually has the best overview of topics like this\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.5},{\"vid\":\"eGnH0KAXhCw\",\"title\":\"Why “No Problem” Can Seem Rude: Phatic Expressions\",\"channel\":\"Tom Scott\",\"summary\":\"Tom Scott explains phatic expressions such as hello, thank you and how are you, which carry social meaning rather than information, and why replies like no problem can seem rude to some people.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN uses it as the short, clear explainer when discussions about greetings and small talk come up.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"phatic expressions\",\"categories\":[\"Language & linguistics\"],\"tags\":[\"linguistics\",\"small talk\",\"greetings\",\"politeness\",\"tom scott\"],\"quote\":\"Tom Scott has an excellent video that addresses this very issue.\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":2.5},{\"vid\":\"ePA1zq56J1I\",\"title\":\"Lecture by Douglas Hofstadter: Albert Einstein on Light; Light on Albert Einstein\",\"channel\":\"Uppsala universitet\",\"summary\":\"Douglas Hofstadter lectures at Uppsala University on how analogy and daring thinking drove Einstein's discovery of light quanta. He argues deep insight in physics comes from imaginative leaps rather than rigid logic.\",\"why_hn\":\"Cited in discussions of analogy-making in science, and revisited by fans of Hofstadter.\",\"content_type\":\"lecture\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"analogy in physics\",\"categories\":[\"Fundamental physics\",\"Consciousness & cognition\",\"University lectures & courses\"],\"tags\":[\"douglas hofstadter\",\"einstein\",\"analogy\",\"light quanta\",\"scientific discovery\"],\"quote\":\"that I often revisit\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.5},{\"vid\":\"eUHBPuHS-7s\",\"title\":\"Epic 2014\",\"channel\":\"jessanmur\",\"summary\":\"Epic 2014 is a short science-fiction film that imagines the media landscape merging into a personalized, computer-generated news service. It is a fictional history of 'Googlezon' and the decline of traditional newspapers.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN returns to it as an uncannily prescient prediction of tech consolidation and AI-written, personalized news.\",\"content_type\":\"other\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"future of media\",\"categories\":[\"Media, journalism & propaganda\",\"Futurism & technology and society\",\"Tech company stories & documentaries\"],\"tags\":[\"googlezon\",\"personalized news\",\"ai-generated news\",\"tech consolidation\",\"speculative fiction\"],\"quote\":\"Rewatching it now gives me this uncanny feeling.\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.5},{\"vid\":\"eW-OMR-iWOE\",\"title\":\"Honest Government Ad | Anti Encryption Law\",\"channel\":\"thejuicemedia\",\"summary\":\"A satirical 'honest' government ad from The Juice Media about Australia's 2018 Assistance and Access anti-encryption bill. It lays out in blunt terms what the law would let authorities do.\",\"why_hn\":\"Commenters recommend it as an entertaining, accessible explanation of how bad the law is, including for non-technical audiences.\",\"content_type\":\"comedy\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"australian anti-encryption law\",\"categories\":[\"Satire & parody\",\"Privacy, surveillance & cybercrime\",\"Cryptography\"],\"tags\":[\"encryption\",\"satire\",\"australia\",\"privacy\",\"surveillance\"],\"quote\":\"It's very entertaining, and explains it in a way that everyday people can understand how bad it will be.\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":2.5},{\"vid\":\"eiYoBbEZwlk\",\"title\":\"Saw Stop - This guy puts a finger into an active table saw blade & comes away without a scratch!\",\"channel\":\"Anthony Prezutti Comedy Mentalist\",\"summary\":\"A short clip showing a person touching an active table saw blade with a finger and walking away unharmed, thanks to SawStop's system that stops the blade within milliseconds of skin contact.\",\"why_hn\":\"Linked as the canonical demo of a safety technology that stops a blade before it injures a finger.\",\"content_type\":\"demo\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"sawstop safety\",\"categories\":[\"Woodworking, metalworking & workshop skills\",\"Engineering & making (other)\"],\"tags\":[\"sawstop\",\"table saw\",\"safety engineering\",\"woodworking\",\"demo\"],\"quote\":\"The demo also never gets old. Just too badass.\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.5},{\"vid\":\"er_lLvkklsk\",\"title\":\"Barliman: trying the halting problem backwards, blindfolded - William Byrd, Greg Rosenblatt\",\"channel\":\"ClojureTV\",\"summary\":\"A Clojure/conj 2016 talk demoing Barliman, a prototype smart editor that does program synthesis. Given a partial program and tests, it completes the program using a relational interpreter written in miniKanren.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN people point to it as an amazing demonstration of relational programming and program synthesis that still looks exciting after LLM code generation.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"program synthesis\",\"categories\":[\"Functional programming\",\"Logic & formal methods\",\"Testing, debugging & developer tools\"],\"tags\":[\"minikanren\",\"logic programming\",\"barliman\",\"clojure\",\"relational interpreter\"],\"quote\":\"I work on miniKanren, which is a logic programming language with a complete search that doesn't hit the nontermination issues you mention.\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":2.5},{\"vid\":\"es6U00LMmC4\",\"title\":\"Best Speech You Will Ever Hear - Gary Yourofsky\",\"channel\":\"TheAnimalHolocaust\",\"summary\":\"Gary Yourofsky's 2010 lecture at Georgia Tech arguing for veganism on ethical, health and environmental grounds. It is a long, forceful animal-rights speech.\",\"why_hn\":\"Some commenters credit it with persuading them to go vegan, while others dismiss parts of it as pseudoscience.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"veganism and animal ethics\",\"categories\":[\"Philosophy & ethics\",\"Social issues & culture\",\"Nutrition & diet science\"],\"tags\":[\"veganism\",\"animal rights\",\"ethics\",\"gary yourofsky\",\"persuasion\"],\"quote\":\"the logical inconsistencies become very apparent\",\"recommenders\":1,\"score\":2.5},{\"vid\":\"ewsGmhAjjjI\",\"title\":\"I have APHANTASIA (and you may too...without realising it!)\",\"channel\":\"JAMIEvstheVOID\",\"summary\":\"An artist describes discovering she has aphantasia, the inability to form mental images, and how it affects her work. She asks viewers about their own visualization.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN points to it as a vivid first-person description of aphantasia and an example of an aphantasic artist.\",\"content_type\":\"commentary\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"aphantasia\",\"categories\":[\"Consciousness & cognition\",\"Neuroscience & the brain\"],\"tags\":[\"aphantasia\",\"mental imagery\",\"visualization\",\"art\"],\"quote\":\"this video is fantastic for describing the feeling of aphantasia\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.5},{\"vid\":\"ezqwfha-BZ8\",\"title\":\"The Fantastic Case of the Missing Tesla\",\"channel\":\"Rich Rebuilds\",\"summary\":\"The final chapter of Rich Rebuilds' saga about buying a used Tesla Model X that went missing, with cameo appearances and the end of the dispute. It is part of a longer series on the problems he had with Tesla.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN recommends the series as a cautionary tale about buying used Teslas and dealing with Tesla service.\",\"content_type\":\"documentary\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"tesla used car saga\",\"categories\":[\"Cars, EVs & motorcycles\",\"Documentaries & storytelling\"],\"tags\":[\"tesla\",\"model x\",\"used cars\",\"customer service\",\"repair\"],\"quote\":\"Anybody involved with Tesla in any way should at least watch\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.5},{\"vid\":\"fTznEIZRkLg\",\"title\":\"Hans Rosling: Global population growth, box by box\",\"channel\":\"TED\",\"summary\":\"Hans Rosling's TED@Cannes talk uses boxes and animated data graphics to show how world population will grow to about 9 billion. He argues that raising living standards for the poorest is what reduces population growth.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN points to it as a data-driven, worldview-changing explanation of why global population will level off.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"global population growth\",\"categories\":[\"Data visualization & information design\",\"Social issues & culture\"],\"tags\":[\"hans rosling\",\"demographics\",\"child mortality\",\"data visualization\",\"development\"],\"quote\":\"Totally changed (well, confirmed) my world view. Start here\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.5},{\"vid\":\"folTvNDL08A\",\"title\":\"David Deutsch: A new way to explain explanation\",\"channel\":\"TED\",\"summary\":\"Physicist David Deutsch's TED talk on why science took off, arguing that good explanations are those that are hard to vary. It contrasts scientific explanation with myth.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN points to it as a short, tight introduction to Deutsch's idea of hard-to-vary explanations.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"philosophy of explanation\",\"categories\":[\"Scientific method & science communication\",\"Philosophy & ethics\"],\"tags\":[\"david deutsch\",\"good explanations\",\"epistemology\",\"scientific method\",\"ted\"],\"quote\":\"it's a very tight talk and you should start from the beginning\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.5},{\"vid\":\"g0lrIi0ce5E\",\"title\":\"Riot On Documentary (2002)\",\"channel\":\"Caroline bruins \",\"summary\":\"A documentary about Riot Entertainment, a Finnish dot-com-era startup that raised millions in funding and then collapsed. It follows the hype-driven rise and implosion of the company.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN recommends it as an entertaining dot-com-era story and a cautionary tale about VC funding and fake-it-till-you-make-it growth.\",\"content_type\":\"documentary\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"dot-com startup collapse\",\"categories\":[\"Startups & entrepreneurship\",\"Documentaries & storytelling\",\"Tech company stories & documentaries\"],\"tags\":[\"riot entertainment\",\"dot-com bubble\",\"venture capital\",\"startups\",\"finland\"],\"quote\":\"I highly recommend the documentary \\\"Riot On!\\\". Great documentary, great cinema, and great entertainment.\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.5},{\"vid\":\"g1GgnbN9oNw\",\"title\":\"The Encryption Tightrope: Balancing Americans’ Security and Privacy: EventID=104573\",\"channel\":\"House Committee on the Judiciary\",\"summary\":\"A 2016 House Judiciary Committee hearing on encryption, held during the Apple and FBI iPhone dispute. It features testimony from Apple, the FBI and outside experts including Susan Landau, and runs over five hours.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN users cite it as primary-source testimony, especially for the argument that weakening encryption is security versus security, not privacy versus security.\",\"content_type\":\"news\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"encryption policy\",\"categories\":[\"Cryptography\",\"Privacy, surveillance & cybercrime\",\"Law, policing & justice\"],\"tags\":[\"apple vs fbi\",\"congressional hearing\",\"backdoors\",\"susan landau\",\"san bernardino\"],\"quote\":\"the recent House Judiciary Committee Hearing is worth the watch\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":2.5},{\"vid\":\"gLDYtH1RH-U\",\"title\":\"Shanghai Tower (650 meters)\",\"channel\":\"On The Roofs\",\"summary\":\"A POV video of climbers illegally scaling the 650 m Shanghai Tower while it was under construction, filmed on a helmet camera.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN recommends it as a gripping and vertigo-inducing watch that put rooftop climbers on the map.\",\"content_type\":\"other\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"rooftopping\",\"categories\":[\"Civil engineering & construction\",\"Sports & athletics\"],\"tags\":[\"shanghai tower\",\"urban climbing\",\"skyscrapers\",\"pov\",\"gopro\"],\"quote\":\"An absolutely fantastic watch.\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.5},{\"vid\":\"gcS04BI2sbk\",\"title\":\"Reinventing Organizations\",\"channel\":\"Reinventing Organizations\",\"summary\":\"Frederic Laloux presents his research on self-managing, purpose-driven organizations, followed by Q&A. He summarizes the findings of his book Reinventing Organizations and examples such as Buurtzorg.\",\"why_hn\":\"Recommended as the best introduction to self-management and new management paradigms.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"self-managing organizations\",\"categories\":[\"Management, leadership & organizations\",\"Tech pioneers & interviews\"],\"tags\":[\"self-management\",\"teal organizations\",\"management\",\"buurtzorg\",\"organizational culture\"],\"quote\":\"I can highly recommend watching this video if you're interested in self-management and the idea of a new management paradigm\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":2.5},{\"vid\":\"ge7i60GuNRg\",\"title\":\"What Would You Do? Bike Theft (White Guy, Black Guy, Pretty Girl)\",\"channel\":\"VladCantSleep\",\"summary\":\"A hidden-camera social experiment in a park where three people try to steal a bike in the open: a white teenager, a black teenager and a young woman. It records how bystanders react to each.\",\"why_hn\":\"Used in threads on bias and social engineering as a vivid example of how bystanders treat different thieves.\",\"content_type\":\"demo\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"bystander bias experiment\",\"categories\":[\"Psychology & human behavior\",\"Social issues & culture\"],\"tags\":[\"social experiment\",\"bias\",\"bike theft\",\"social engineering\",\"hidden camera\"],\"quote\":\"There's an awesome video of three college-student-aged in a park.\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.5},{\"vid\":\"gn8m5d74fk8\",\"title\":\"Oculus Connect Keynote: John Carmack\",\"channel\":\"Meta VR\",\"summary\":\"John Carmack's keynote at Oculus Connect 2014 about the Gear VR and development stories from building it. He discusses mobile GPU optimization, latency, and display ideas like programmable interlacing.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN recommends it for Carmack's detailed engineering insight into VR rendering and latency challenges.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"advanced\",\"primary_topic\":\"vr rendering and latency\",\"categories\":[\"VR, AR & spatial computing\",\"Software performance & optimization\",\"Tech pioneers & interviews\"],\"tags\":[\"john carmack\",\"oculus\",\"gear vr\",\"mobile gpu\",\"latency\"],\"quote\":\"Carmack's 2014 Oculus Connect keynote is well worth watching\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.5},{\"vid\":\"gp4U5aH_T6A\",\"title\":\"Saifedean Ammous: Bitcoin, Anarchy, and Austrian Economics | Lex Fridman Podcast #284\",\"channel\":\"Lex Fridman\",\"summary\":\"A long Lex Fridman podcast conversation with Austrian economist Saifedean Ammous, author of The Bitcoin Standard. They cover Bitcoin, fiat money, anarchy and Austrian economics.\",\"why_hn\":\"Cited as a thorough statement of the bitcoin-maximalist case, with the host pushing back.\",\"content_type\":\"podcast\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"bitcoin and austrian economics\",\"categories\":[\"Cryptography\",\"Macroeconomics & financial crises\",\"Microeconomics & behavioral economics\"],\"tags\":[\"bitcoin\",\"austrian economics\",\"fiat money\",\"saifedean ammous\",\"lex fridman\"],\"quote\":\"this episode turned me from a \\\"fuck any form of crypto\\\" stance to an appreciation of BTC the technology\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.5},{\"vid\":\"hCQCP-5g5bo\",\"title\":\"I Saved a PNG Image To A Bird\",\"channel\":\"Benn Jordan\",\"summary\":\"Benn Jordan's video about storing a PNG image in a living bird, a starling that learns to reproduce encoded sounds. It mixes ornithology, audio engineering, and data encoding.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN fans point to it as a fun, nerdy crossover of bird song acoustics and technology, and the story itself got its own thread.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"data storage in birds\",\"categories\":[\"Animals & nature\",\"Audio & video engineering\",\"Documentaries & storytelling\"],\"tags\":[\"benn jordan\",\"starling\",\"bird song\",\"audio encoding\",\"ornithology\"],\"quote\":\"you might enjoy Benn Jordan's video of \\\"saving\\\" a PNG to a bird\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.5},{\"vid\":\"hIZxTQP1ifo\",\"title\":\"Edward Kmett - Type Classes vs. the World\",\"channel\":\"Boston Haskell\",\"summary\":\"Edward Kmett speaks at the Boston Haskell meetup about type classes and the design tradeoffs of global coherence compared with other approaches to implicit instances. It covers why uniqueness of instances matters for reasoning and refactoring.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN points to it as the definitive explanation of why coherence and the orphan rule matter, in debates over Haskell, Rust traits, OCaml modules and Elm.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"advanced\",\"primary_topic\":\"type classes\",\"categories\":[\"Programming language design\",\"Functional programming\"],\"tags\":[\"haskell\",\"type classes\",\"coherence\",\"orphan rule\",\"edward kmett\",\"traits\"],\"quote\":\"Ed Kmett's fantastic \\\"Typeclasses v. the World\\\" talk covers\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.5},{\"vid\":\"hckwxq8rnr0\",\"title\":\"Apollo Core Rope Memory (Apollo Guidance Computer Part 30)\",\"channel\":\"CuriousMarc\",\"summary\":\"CuriousMarc's Apollo Guidance Computer restoration series looks at core rope memory, the ROM that held the Moon landing programs. Mike Stewart builds a custom reader to recover lost AGC programs.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN commenters recommend it as the deepest explanation of how AGC rope memory works and how it differs from core memory.\",\"content_type\":\"documentary\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"apollo guidance computer memory\",\"categories\":[\"History of computing\",\"Space exploration & spaceflight\",\"Demoscene & retrocomputing\"],\"tags\":[\"core rope memory\",\"apollo guidance computer\",\"vintage computing\",\"restoration\",\"rom\"],\"quote\":\"Here,s a deep, deep dive into AGC rope memory.\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.5},{\"vid\":\"hhMAt3BluAU\",\"title\":\"Trump's Biggest Failure\",\"channel\":\"Kraut\",\"summary\":\"A long video essay by Kraut arguing that Trump's biggest failure was his handling of China. It spends much of its length on Chinese history, culture, the trade war, and the rise of a communist superpower.\",\"why_hn\":\"Commenters point to it as a well-researched explainer of the history and culture behind China's current position, despite the political title.\",\"content_type\":\"commentary\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"china geopolitics\",\"categories\":[\"Geopolitics & foreign policy\",\"US politics & elections\",\"World history\"],\"tags\":[\"china\",\"trade war\",\"history\",\"foreign policy\",\"tibet\"],\"quote\":\"Kraut has a fantastic video on the topic\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.5},{\"vid\":\"hk-0qJXyido\",\"title\":\"Nord Stream sabotage and hybrid war on Europe\",\"channel\":\"Anders Puck Nielsen\",\"summary\":\"Anders Puck Nielsen analyzes the Nord Stream pipeline sabotage using Kilcullen's theory of liminal warfare and prospect theory. He argues from the operational design that Russia is the most likely culprit, then discusses how hybrid warfare might be used against Europe.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN points to it as a compact, reasoned case for Russian responsibility, though at least one commenter found the argument unconvincing.\",\"content_type\":\"commentary\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"nord stream sabotage\",\"categories\":[\"Geopolitics & foreign policy\",\"Military history & warfare\"],\"tags\":[\"hybrid warfare\",\"nord stream\",\"russia\",\"geopolitics\",\"military analysis\"],\"quote\":\"Anders Puck Nielsen has an under 15 minute video with a compelling explanation for why Russia is most likely to have done it\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.5},{\"vid\":\"hyYCn_kAngI\",\"title\":\"How to Get Your First Customers | Startup School\",\"channel\":\"Y Combinator\",\"summary\":\"A Startup School talk by YC partner and former Airbnb growth head Gustaf Alstromer on how startups get their first customers. It covers doing things that don't scale, founders learning sales, the sales funnel, and charging your first customer.\",\"why_hn\":\"Commenters recommend the whole talk as practical, tactical advice for early customer acquisition and outbound sales.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"intro\",\"primary_topic\":\"getting first customers\",\"categories\":[\"Startups & entrepreneurship\",\"Product, marketing & sales\"],\"tags\":[\"startups\",\"sales\",\"growth\",\"y combinator\",\"b2b\"],\"quote\":\"The entire video is really good actually I recommend watching the entire thing.\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.5},{\"vid\":\"i9i47sgi-V4\",\"title\":\"How Corruption Destroys Armies - Theft, Graft, and Russian failure in Ukraine\",\"channel\":\"Perun\",\"summary\":\"Perun analyzes how corruption and theft in defence procurement hollowed out the Russian military before its invasion of Ukraine. It explains the mechanics of graft and how it degrades capability.\",\"why_hn\":\"Recommended as a long but insightful explanation of how corruption works inside institutions.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"military corruption\",\"categories\":[\"Military history & warfare\",\"Geopolitics & foreign policy\"],\"tags\":[\"russia\",\"ukraine\",\"procurement\",\"corruption\",\"defense economics\"],\"quote\":\"Both these videos are long, but they had a lot of interesting ideas and insight on this topic\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.5},{\"vid\":\"iIpPuJ_r8Xg\",\"title\":\"The US Military’s Massive Global Transportation System\",\"channel\":\"Wendover Productions\",\"summary\":\"Wendover Productions explains how the US military moves people and materiel worldwide, including prepositioned equipment, sealift and airlift. It shows the scale of the logistics system behind US force projection.\",\"why_hn\":\"Recommended as a clear overview of military logistics, often as a contrast with civilian infrastructure efforts.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"military logistics\",\"categories\":[\"Military history & warfare\",\"Business & economics (other)\",\"Ships, submarines & maritime\"],\"tags\":[\"us military\",\"supply chain\",\"transportation\",\"prepositioning\",\"wendover\"],\"quote\":\"Wendover Productions has a great video about the insane amount of logistics\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.5},{\"vid\":\"iLmkec_4Rfo\",\"title\":\"David Carr vs. Some Guys from VICE\",\"channel\":\"AudenRaybourn\",\"summary\":\"A clip from the documentary Page One in which New York Times reporter David Carr interviews and confronts the founders of Vice magazine over their media deal. It captures tension between old and new media in 2010.\",\"why_hn\":\"Brought up whenever Vice is discussed, as a memorable scene of Carr pressing its founders.\",\"content_type\":\"interview\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"vice and traditional media\",\"categories\":[\"Media, journalism & propaganda\",\"Documentaries & storytelling\"],\"tags\":[\"david carr\",\"vice\",\"page one\",\"journalism\",\"new york times\"],\"quote\":\"One of the best scenes from Page One\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.5},{\"vid\":\"ieb1lmm9xHk\",\"title\":\"Inner Game of Tennis\",\"channel\":\"TheCoach\",\"summary\":\"A 1970 demonstration of W. Timothy Gallwey, author of The Inner Game of Tennis, teaching a complete beginner to play tennis in about ten minutes. He chats with her, feeds balls and gives positive feedback instead of instruction.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN commenters use it as a vivid demonstration of learning by quieting the conscious mind, and recommend it alongside the book.\",\"content_type\":\"demo\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"inner game of tennis\",\"categories\":[\"Education & learning\",\"Productivity & self-improvement\",\"Sports & athletics\"],\"tags\":[\"timothy gallwey\",\"coaching\",\"learning\",\"tennis\",\"feedback\"],\"quote\":\"This video of Timothy Gallwey teaching a woman how to play tennis. In 5 minutes.\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.5},{\"vid\":\"ip641WmY4pA\",\"title\":\"DIY haptic input knob: BLDC motor + round LCD\",\"channel\":\"scottbez1\",\"summary\":\"A two-minute demo of SmartKnob View, an open-source input knob built from a brushless gimbal motor, magnetic encoder and round LCD. Closed-loop torque control gives software-defined detents and end stops.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN people hold it up as a polished solo hardware project and the go-to example of haptic knobs, including in discussions of physical car controls.\",\"content_type\":\"demo\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"haptic input devices\",\"categories\":[\"Embedded systems & DIY electronics\",\"3D printing, CNC & maker projects\"],\"tags\":[\"smartknob\",\"bldc motor\",\"esp32\",\"haptic feedback\",\"open-source hardware\"],\"quote\":\"I made a rotary input device that provides software-defined \\\"virtual\\\" detents and end-stops, implemented using a BLDC gimbal motor.\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.5},{\"vid\":\"iphcyNWFD10\",\"title\":\"The Absurdity of Detecting Gravitational Waves\",\"channel\":\"Veritasium\",\"summary\":\"Veritasium explains in detail how LIGO detects gravitational waves, with a laser interferometer measuring displacements smaller than a proton. The video focuses on the extreme precision and the techniques needed rather than the general discovery story.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN recommends it as a good layperson explanation of how LIGO's detection works and why it is so hard.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"gravitational wave detection\",\"categories\":[\"Cosmology & astrophysics\",\"Fundamental physics\"],\"tags\":[\"ligo\",\"gravitational waves\",\"interferometer\",\"veritasium\",\"physics\"],\"quote\":\"Here is a great video with explanations\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":2.5},{\"vid\":\"iqddnwKF8HQ\",\"title\":\"Zig 2026: No-AI Policy, \$670K Foundation, Left GitHub & Why Zig Isn’t 1.0 - Andrew Kelley Explains\",\"channel\":\"JetBrains\",\"summary\":\"JetBrains interviews Zig creator Andrew Kelley about why Zig has no 1.0 after a decade, why the project left GitHub, and why it bans AI contributions. He also covers what makes Zig better than C and his views on open source.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN commenters point to it as a convincing primary-source interview showing Zig's cohesive design vision and the creator's level-headed reasoning.\",\"content_type\":\"interview\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"zig programming language\",\"categories\":[\"C, C++, Rust, Go & systems languages\",\"Software practice, open source & careers\",\"Tech pioneers & interviews\"],\"tags\":[\"zig\",\"andrew kelley\",\"systems programming\",\"open source\",\"ai policy\"],\"quote\":\"convinced me more than any design doc or blogpost could\",\"recommenders\":5,\"score\":2.5},{\"vid\":\"j6ow-UemzBc\",\"title\":\"Design Microservice Architectures the Right Way\",\"channel\":\"InfoQ\",\"summary\":\"Michael Bryzek of Flow gives a QCon London 2018 talk on key decisions for building maintainable microservices. It covers infrastructure, continuous deployment, communication, event streaming and language choice.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN commenters recommend it for showing the tooling possible when schemas and APIs are treated as code.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"microservice architecture\",\"categories\":[\"Software architecture & design\",\"Cloud, DevOps & reliability\"],\"tags\":[\"microservices\",\"continuous delivery\",\"api schemas\",\"event streaming\",\"qcon\"],\"quote\":\"There's a great talk that I highly recommend about some of the magic you can do\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.5},{\"vid\":\"jAhjPd4uNFY\",\"title\":\"Genetic Engineering Will Change Everything Forever – CRISPR\",\"channel\":\"Kurzgesagt – In a Nutshell\",\"summary\":\"Kurzgesagt's animated explainer on CRISPR gene editing, covering how the technology works and what it could mean for curing disease, designer babies and aging. It frames genetic engineering as an irreversible change coming to humanity.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN commenters hand it out as a quick, accessible primer whenever CRISPR or gene editing comes up.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"crispr gene editing\",\"categories\":[\"Evolution & genetics\",\"Biology & biotechnology\"],\"tags\":[\"crispr\",\"cas9\",\"genetic engineering\",\"designer babies\",\"animation\"],\"quote\":\"I strongly recommend this quick introduction video from Kurzgesagt on YouTube\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.5},{\"vid\":\"jhicDUgXyNg\",\"title\":\"Delvon Lamarr Organ Trio - Warm-up Set (Live on KEXP)\",\"channel\":\"KEXP\",\"summary\":\"A live KEXP warm-up set by the Delvon Lamarr Organ Trio, recorded at Upstream Music Fest in 2017. The set includes Move On Up and Memphis.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN people recommend it as a great live KEXP session with standout guitar work and good sound.\",\"content_type\":\"music\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"live organ trio\",\"categories\":[\"Music performance & songs\"],\"tags\":[\"kexp\",\"soul jazz\",\"organ trio\",\"live session\",\"seattle\"],\"quote\":\"He's hands down one of the most talented guitarists alive today.\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.5},{\"vid\":\"jhnKBKZvb_U\",\"title\":\"Why is Time a One-Way Street?\",\"channel\":\"Santa Fe Institute\",\"summary\":\"Leonard Susskind's Santa Fe Institute talk on the arrow of time: why the past differs from the future when physics equations are time-symmetric. He covers entropy, cosmology and Boltzmann brains.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN commenters recommend it as a clear explanation of why time runs one way, from a leading physicist.\",\"content_type\":\"lecture\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"arrow of time\",\"categories\":[\"Fundamental physics\",\"Cosmology & astrophysics\"],\"tags\":[\"leonard susskind\",\"entropy\",\"cosmology\",\"boltzmann brains\",\"theoretical physics\"],\"quote\":\"Highly recommend the talk.\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.5},{\"vid\":\"kgCUn4fQTsc\",\"title\":\"Google Engineer on His Sentient AI Claim\",\"channel\":\"Bloomberg Tech\",\"summary\":\"Bloomberg Technology interviews Google engineer Blake Lemoine about the experiments that led him to believe LaMDA was sentient and why he was placed on administrative leave. He also raises concerns about AI ethics at Google.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN commenters recommend watching it to hear his side directly, noting he comes across as coherent, while others dispute his sincerity.\",\"content_type\":\"interview\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"lamda sentience claim\",\"categories\":[\"AI safety, AGI & impact\",\"LLMs & generative AI\",\"Consciousness & cognition\"],\"tags\":[\"blake lemoine\",\"lamda\",\"google\",\"ai sentience\",\"ai ethics\"],\"quote\":\"I'd implore anyone reading this thread to see what he had to say for yourself and form your own opinion\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":2.5},{\"vid\":\"l9ag2x3CS9M\",\"title\":\"Why Japan had NO Chance in WW2\",\"channel\":\"Military History Visualized\",\"summary\":\"Military History Visualized charts ship production by the United States and Japan from December 1941 to September 1945. The growing numbers show why Japan, despite a stronger starting navy, could not win a long war.\",\"why_hn\":\"Cited as one of the best visualizations of how overwhelmingly dominant US industrial output was in the Pacific war.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"wwii pacific naval production\",\"categories\":[\"Military history & warfare\",\"Ships, submarines & maritime\"],\"tags\":[\"world war ii\",\"industrial capacity\",\"imperial japanese navy\",\"us navy\",\"shipbuilding\"],\"quote\":\"One of the best visualizations I've come across of just how dominant the US industrial base was in the 1940s under full mobilization.\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":2.5},{\"vid\":\"lC4YLMLar5I\",\"title\":\"Elite: \\\"The game that couldn't be written\\\"\",\"channel\":\"Alexander the ok\",\"summary\":\"An hour-long video essay on Elite, the 1984 BBC Micro game by David Braben and Ian Bell. It covers how they fit a 3D engine, economy and universe into 22KB on a 2MHz 6502.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN commenters recommend it as an amazing overview of the technical feats and history behind Elite, and cite it for what the 6502 could do.\",\"content_type\":\"documentary\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"history of the game Elite\",\"categories\":[\"Game history & retro gaming\",\"Demoscene & retrocomputing\",\"Computer graphics & rendering\"],\"tags\":[\"elite\",\"bbc micro\",\"6502\",\"retro games\",\"3d graphics\"],\"quote\":\"has an amazing video on this\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.5},{\"vid\":\"lFXJWPhDsSY\",\"title\":\"Alpha Zero's \\\"Immortal Zugzwang Game\\\" against Stockfish\",\"channel\":\"agadmator's Chess Channel\",\"summary\":\"agadmator walks through a game in which DeepMind's AlphaZero beat Stockfish, ending in a famous zugzwang that leaves the engine helpless. He gives commentary on the moves.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN recommends it as a striking, well-explained example of AlphaZero's play and of zugzwang.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"intro\",\"primary_topic\":\"alphazero vs stockfish chess\",\"categories\":[\"Chess, board games & puzzles\",\"Machine learning & deep learning\"],\"tags\":[\"alphazero\",\"stockfish\",\"zugzwang\",\"chess\",\"deepmind\"],\"quote\":\"A great example I love showing people is Alpha Zero's infamous \\\"Immortal Zugzwang Game\\\" against Stockfish\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.5},{\"vid\":\"lX-K63pVPTM\",\"title\":\"David Deutsch on Optimism\",\"channel\":\"Royal Society of Arts\",\"summary\":\"An excerpt from an RSA event in which physicist David Deutsch makes the case for optimism as a driver of progress in the 21st century. It is a short highlight of a longer discussion.\",\"why_hn\":\"Pointed to as an antidote to pessimism about the future, tied to Deutsch's ideas in The Beginning of Infinity.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"optimism and progress\",\"categories\":[\"Futurism & technology and society\",\"Philosophy & ethics\"],\"tags\":[\"david deutsch\",\"optimism\",\"enlightenment\",\"knowledge\",\"future\"],\"quote\":\"I encourage everyone pessimistic about our future to learn about David Deutsch's infinite optimism\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.5},{\"vid\":\"lqJUIqZNzP8\",\"title\":\"Avoiding Negative Side Effects: Concrete Problems in AI Safety part 1\",\"channel\":\"Robert Miles AI Safety \",\"summary\":\"Robert Miles introduces the first of several videos on the paper 'Concrete Problems in AI Safety', focusing on how AI systems can cause accidental negative side effects. It explains the problem in accessible terms.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN recommends Robert Miles' channel as a clear starting point for people curious about AI safety.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"intro\",\"primary_topic\":\"ai safety\",\"categories\":[\"AI safety, AGI & impact\"],\"tags\":[\"negative side effects\",\"concrete problems in ai safety\",\"ai risk\",\"robert miles\",\"alignment\"],\"quote\":\"For those curious about AI safety I heavily recommend Robert Miles channel on YouTube.\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.5},{\"vid\":\"m1lhGqNCZlA\",\"title\":\"DEF CON 24 - Chris Rock - How to Overthrow a Government\",\"channel\":\"DEFCONConference\",\"summary\":\"A DEF CON 24 talk on how a cyber mercenary group could forge identities and create the conditions for overthrowing a government. It is entertainingly outlandish and includes a drone-mounted saw for cutting power lines.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN recommends it as an amazing, entertaining talk and cites it in threads on power-line sabotage and coup tactics.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"regime change tactics\",\"categories\":[\"Security & hacking\",\"Geopolitics & foreign policy\"],\"tags\":[\"def con\",\"coups\",\"drones\",\"hacking\",\"security\"],\"quote\":\"If you've not seen this amazing talk I can't recommend it enough.\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.5},{\"vid\":\"mPZn4x3uOac\",\"title\":\"In The Bleak Midwinter - Jacob Collier\",\"channel\":\"Jacob Collier\",\"summary\":\"Jacob Collier layers ten vocal parts to arrange and perform Harold Darke's carol \\\"In the Bleak Midwinter\\\", with inventive harmony and tuning.\",\"why_hn\":\"Recommended as a showcase of Collier's harmonic and microtonal skill.\",\"content_type\":\"music\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"jacob collier harmony\",\"categories\":[\"Music performance & songs\",\"Music theory, synthesis & production\"],\"tags\":[\"jacob collier\",\"a cappella\",\"microtonal\",\"christmas carol\",\"harmony\"],\"quote\":\"Probably the best example, especially the middle\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.5},{\"vid\":\"mPn2AdMH7UQ\",\"title\":\"Surreal Numbers (writing the first book) - Numberphile\",\"channel\":\"Numberphile\",\"summary\":\"A Numberphile interview with Donald Knuth about how he came to write the first book on surreal numbers after a lunch with John Conway. He tells the story casually in about 14 minutes.\",\"why_hn\":\"Recommended as a short, charming introduction to surreal numbers and to how Knuth wrote his book in under a week.\",\"content_type\":\"interview\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"surreal numbers\",\"categories\":[\"Recreational & visual math\",\"Tech pioneers & interviews\"],\"tags\":[\"donald knuth\",\"john conway\",\"surreal numbers\",\"numberphile\",\"mathematics history\"],\"quote\":\"This interview is excellent\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":2.5},{\"vid\":\"mSgXWpvQEHE\",\"title\":\"Keynote. Professor Steven G. Johnson | JuliaCon 2019\",\"channel\":\"The Julia Programming Language\",\"summary\":\"Steven G. Johnson, MIT professor and FFTW co-author, gives a JuliaCon 2019 keynote on metaprogramming and staged programming in Julia, showing how it enables high-performance numerical code and when not to use macros.\",\"why_hn\":\"Cited for showing how Julia's metaprogramming can beat C and Fortran, along with sound advice not to overuse it.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"advanced\",\"primary_topic\":\"julia metaprogramming\",\"categories\":[\"Python, Ruby & scripting languages\",\"Programming language design\",\"Software performance & optimization\"],\"tags\":[\"julia\",\"metaprogramming\",\"high performance computing\",\"macros\",\"numerical computing\"],\"quote\":\"really interesting, informative, entertaining and well delivered.\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.5},{\"vid\":\"mUcUy7SqdS0\",\"title\":\"Glass engineering - designing and making photochromic glass\",\"channel\":\"Applied Science\",\"summary\":\"Ben Krasnow of Applied Science shows how to make small batches of specialty glass with minimal equipment, including designing and making photochromic glass. He covers ingredients, melting and the challenges involved.\",\"why_hn\":\"Recommended as a hands-on introduction to glass melting and chemistry and to Krasnow's channel.\",\"content_type\":\"tutorial\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"glass making\",\"categories\":[\"Materials science\",\"Chemistry\",\"Woodworking, metalworking & workshop skills\"],\"tags\":[\"photochromic glass\",\"ben krasnow\",\"materials\",\"diy\",\"chemistry\"],\"quote\":\"I'd highly recommend his channel to anyone interested in science and fabrication.\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.5},{\"vid\":\"mb3uK-_QkOo\",\"title\":\"We Are The Art | Brandon Sanderson’s Keynote Speech\",\"channel\":\"Brandon Sanderson\",\"summary\":\"Brandon Sanderson's keynote on AI-generated art, arguing that the artistic process and the journey matter more than the finished product. He explains why he rebels against generative AI in creative work.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN commenters share it as an eloquent argument that AI output is not art, and as a companion to worries about losing deep thinking.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"ai and art\",\"categories\":[\"LLMs & generative AI\",\"Literature & writing craft\",\"AI safety, AGI & impact\"],\"tags\":[\"ai art\",\"creativity\",\"brandon sanderson\",\"generative ai\",\"writing\"],\"quote\":\"Here is author Brandon Sanderson eloquently explaining why AI generated slop will never be art\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":2.5},{\"vid\":\"meiU6TxysCg\",\"title\":\"Two Monkeys Were Paid Unequally: Excerpt from Frans de Waal's TED Talk\",\"channel\":\"TED Blog Video\",\"summary\":\"A short excerpt from Frans de Waal's TED talk showing a capuchin monkey fairness experiment in which two monkeys are paid unequally, one with cucumber and one with grapes. The shortchanged monkey reacts angrily.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN uses it again and again as shorthand for the idea that resentment of unfair pay and inequality is built into primates, including us.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"fairness in primates\",\"categories\":[\"Animals & nature\",\"Psychology & human behavior\",\"Philosophy & ethics\"],\"tags\":[\"capuchin monkeys\",\"inequity aversion\",\"frans de waal\",\"morality\",\"animal behavior\"],\"quote\":\"This is the video that explains the best\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.5},{\"vid\":\"mmfjM-SGlGs\",\"title\":\"Here I Stand, at Age 80\",\"channel\":\"TheTedNelson\",\"summary\":\"Ted Nelson, the originator of hypertext and Project Xanadu, gives a personal account at age 80 of his ideals, his career, and how a poor career plan led to discoveries and adventures. It works as an alternative history of personal computing and hypertext.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN people point to it as Nelson's candid, first-person overview of his life, Xanadu's failure, and the lessons he drew, a historical record from the man himself.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"history of hypertext\",\"categories\":[\"Tech pioneers & interviews\",\"History of computing\",\"GUI, HCI & interface history\"],\"tags\":[\"ted nelson\",\"xanadu\",\"hypertext\",\"computer history\",\"personal computing\"],\"quote\":\"Strongly recommended, and I'm grateful that he recorded this historical treasure.\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.5},{\"vid\":\"mpbeOCKZFfQ\",\"title\":\"Cambridge Analytica Uncovered: Secret filming reveals election tricks\",\"channel\":\"Channel 4 News\",\"summary\":\"A Channel 4 News undercover investigation in which Cambridge Analytica executives are filmed discussing bribes, honeypots, fake identities and manipulating elections around the world.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN points to it as the primary evidence of what Cambridge Analytica was willing to do, especially in Facebook data scandal threads.\",\"content_type\":\"news\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"cambridge analytica investigation\",\"categories\":[\"Privacy, surveillance & cybercrime\",\"Media, journalism & propaganda\",\"US politics & elections\"],\"tags\":[\"cambridge analytica\",\"election manipulation\",\"undercover\",\"data privacy\",\"facebook\"],\"quote\":\"I highly recommend watching the report, it's a fascinating watch.\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.5},{\"vid\":\"n28W4AmvMDE\",\"title\":\"How Sugar & Processed Foods Impact Your Health | Dr. Robert Lustig\",\"channel\":\"Andrew Huberman\",\"summary\":\"A long Huberman Lab podcast episode with Dr. Robert Lustig on the calories-in, calories-out model and how sugar, fructose, fiber and processed foods affect insulin, liver and metabolic health.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN mentions it mostly as a source for the argument that sugar is toxic, though some commenters push back on claims like fructose being addictive.\",\"content_type\":\"podcast\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"sugar and metabolic health\",\"categories\":[\"Nutrition & diet science\",\"Medicine & infectious disease\"],\"tags\":[\"robert lustig\",\"sugar\",\"fructose\",\"nutrition\",\"metabolism\",\"huberman\"],\"quote\":null,\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.5},{\"vid\":\"nSKp2StlS6s\",\"title\":\"You Give REST a Bad Name\",\"channel\":\"Dylan Beattie\",\"summary\":\"Dylan Beattie's parody of 'You Give Love a Bad Name' about hypermedia APIs and REST, performed with his band at developer conferences.\",\"why_hn\":\"Shared as developer humor, with commenters insisting any Dylan Beattie mention must come with this song.\",\"content_type\":\"music\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"programming parody songs\",\"categories\":[\"Software (other)\",\"Software architecture & design\",\"Satire & parody\"],\"tags\":[\"rest\",\"hypermedia\",\"parody\",\"dylan beattie\",\"developer humor\"],\"quote\":\"You Give REST a Bad Name\\\" is also excellent.\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.5}",
