 of the affiliate tag replacement in browser dev tools.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN treats it as top-tier investigative journalism on YouTube and the video that triggered lawsuits against Honey.\",\"content_type\":\"commentary\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"affiliate marketing scams\",\"categories\":[\"Product, marketing & sales\",\"Web development\",\"Media, journalism & propaganda\"],\"tags\":[\"honey\",\"affiliate fraud\",\"browser extensions\",\"paypal\",\"influencers\",\"investigative\"],\"quote\":\"one of the best pieces of investigative journalism I've seen on youtube\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.5},{\"vid\":\"vq2BxAJZ4Tc\",\"title\":\"Extremely Large Numbers 1 - Introduction\",\"channel\":\"Giroux Studios\",\"summary\":\"The first video in a series on extremely large numbers, introducing the topic with examples. Later parts go deep into the fast-growing hierarchy.\",\"why_hn\":\"Recommended in large-number threads as going further than other popular videos on Graham's number and ordinals.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"intro\",\"primary_topic\":\"extremely large numbers\",\"categories\":[\"Recreational & visual math\",\"Computability & complexity theory\"],\"tags\":[\"googology\",\"graham's number\",\"fast-growing hierarchy\",\"ordinals\"],\"quote\":\"I would also recommend Giroux Studios' 'Extremely Large Numbers'[1]\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.5},{\"vid\":\"w-I6XTVZXww\",\"title\":\"ASTOUNDING: 1 + 2 + 3 + 4 + 5 + ... = -1/12\",\"channel\":\"Numberphile\",\"summary\":\"A Numberphile video in which physicists Tony Padilla and Ed Copeland show a seemingly astounding result that 1+2+3+4+... equals -1/12. The argument is informal and has drawn criticism for glossing over what the result actually means.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN uses it as the standard reference for the -1/12 meme, with commenters split between enjoying it and calling it a cheat.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"divergent series\",\"ca