s Baute inside a sealed homemade biodome as carbon dioxide builds up, showing how stale air with elevated CO2 affects cognitive function. Sources include studies on CO2 and cognitive scores.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN links it as a popular, accessible introduction to indoor CO2 and its effect on thinking, in air quality threads.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"indoor CO2 and cognition\",\"categories\":[\"Neuroscience & the brain\",\"Everyday physics & science demos\",\"Power grid, heating & buildings\"],\"tags\":[\"carbon dioxide\",\"air quality\",\"cognitive function\",\"tom scott\",\"ventilation\"],\"quote\":\"Tom Scott did a great video on it a while back\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.0},{\"vid\":\"1YFrISfN7jo\",\"title\":\"The Geometry of Causality\",\"channel\":\"PBS Space Time\",\"summary\":\"PBS Space Time explains how spacetime geometry and light cones determine the order of events and what can cause what. It visualizes causality in special relativity.\",\"why_hn\":\"Used as a go-to reference for relativity arguments, such as spacetime intervals being the same for all observers, and as a suggested follow-up for physics fans.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"intro\",\"primary_topic\":\"relativity and causality\",\"categories\":[\"Fundamental physics\",\"Cosmology & astrophysics\"],\"tags\":[\"special relativity\",\"light cones\",\"spacetime\",\"causality\",\"physics\"],\"quote\":null,\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.0}",
