d ArenaNet, speaks at HandmadeCon 2015 in a conversation with Casey Muratori. He discusses network code and architecture in games he worked on, including mistakes on Diablo and the success of Guild Wars.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN points to it as a first-hand account of game netcode and engineering lessons from a Blizzard and Guild Wars developer.\",\"content_type\":\"interview\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"game networking\",\"categories\":[\"Game programming & engines\",\"Indie game development\",\"Tech pioneers & interviews\"],\"tags\":[\"netcode\",\"game development\",\"blizzard\",\"diablo\",\"guild wars\",\"handmadecon\"],\"quote\":\"good interview with him talking about screwing up Diablo and doing a good job on Guild Wars\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.0},{\"vid\":\"1rCrfQUcXDI\",\"title\":\"Pinging The Voyager 2 Probe (PART 2)\",\"channel\":\"EEVdiscover\",\"summary\":\"Part two of EEVblog's visit to the NASA/CSIRO Canberra Deep Space Communication Complex, showing the control room and how operators contact Voyager 2. It includes live data and spectrum displays.\",\"why_hn\":\"Commenters recommend the series for hearing an operations supervisor explain how Voyager signals are actually received.\",\"content_type\":\"interview\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"deep space network communications\",\"categories\":[\"Space exploration & spaceflight\",\"Electronics & circuit design\"],\"tags\":[\"voyager 2\",\"deep space network\",\"nasa\",\"radio communications\",\"canberra\"],\"quote\":\"Dave Jones of EEVBlog has a nice series of videos talking to Richard Stephenson, Operations Supervisor at the DSN's Canberra site.\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.0},{\"vid\":\"2-oBNh0UkQc\",\"title\":\"SymbOS MP3MSX Demostration\",\"channel\":\"karloch\",\"summary\":\"A demonstration of SymbOS, a multitasking operating system for 8-bit Z80 machines, running on a real MSX turboR with an MP3MSX card and a CF IDE interface. It shows the OS playing audio and running a graphical desktop on very old hardware, captured from the real machine and not an emulator.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN points to it as a vivid showcase of how much a modern-feeling GUI OS can do on slow 8-bit hardware.\",\"content_type\":\"demo\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"retro computing operating systems\",\"categories\":[\"Demoscene & retrocomputing\",\"Operating systems & kernels\"],\"tags\":[\"symbos\",\"msx\",\"z80\",\"8-bit\",\"retrocomputing\"],\"quote\":\"\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.0},{\"vid\":\"21EiKfQYZXc\",\"title\":\"Andrew Ng: Artificial Intelligence is the New Electricity\",\"channel\":\"Stanford Graduate School of Business\",\"summary\":\"Andrew Ng speaks at the Stanford MSx Future Forum about how AI is transforming industry after industry, comparing its impact to electricity. The talk also touches on evil-AI worries, jobs and basic income.\",\"why_hn\":\"Recommended as a broad, practical view of AI's near-term impact from a leading practitioner, with his argument that worrying about evil AI is premature.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"ai and industry\",\"categories\":[\"AI safety, AGI & impact\",\"Labor, work & inequality\",\"Machine learning & deep learning\"],\"tags\":[\"andrew ng\",\"artificial intelligence\",\"basic income\",\"automation\",\"ai ethics\"],\"quote\":\"I really enjoyed this Andrew Ng talk\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.0},{\"vid\":\"23X14HS4gLk\",\"title\":\"Don't Be a Sucker - 1947\",\"channel\":\"Weirdo Video\",\"summary\":\"A 1947 US military film that deconstructs how the Nazi regime used divisive propaganda and prejudice to split and control a population. It teaches viewers to recognise demagoguery tactics.\",\"why_hn\":\"Shared in political threads as a timeless warning about divisive manipulation and demagogues.\",\"content_type\":\"documentary\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"propaganda and demagoguery\",\"categories\":[\"Media, journalism & 