rely by an unexpanded Commodore VIC-20 and a 1541 disk drive, using only a few kilobytes of RAM and a 16 KB disk. It uses demoscene effects to tell a story.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN recommends it as a showcase of what skilled demoscene programmers can squeeze out of extremely limited hardware.\",\"content_type\":\"demo\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"vic-20 demoscene\",\"categories\":[\"Demoscene & retrocomputing\",\"Music performance & songs\"],\"tags\":[\"demoscene\",\"vic-20\",\"retro computing\",\"8-bit\",\"viznut\"],\"quote\":\"I like that the demo effects are used here to tell a story in addition to being a pure display of coding prowess.\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.0},{\"vid\":\"2U9WMftV40c\",\"title\":\"Rick Roderick on Baudrillard - Fatal Strategies [full length]\",\"channel\":\"The Partially Examined Life\",\"summary\":\"Rick Roderick's 1993 lecture on Baudrillard, the last in his series The Self Under Siege. It covers hyperreality, simulation and what Baudrillard calls fatal strategies.\",\"why_hn\":\"Recommended as a much easier way into Baudrillard's ideas than reading his own writing.\",\"content_type\":\"lecture\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"baudrillard and hyperreality\",\"categories\":[\"Philosophy & ethics\",\"University lectures & courses\"],\"tags\":[\"baudrillard\",\"hyperreality\",\"simulacra\",\"postmodernism\",\"rick roderick\"],\"quote\":\"here's an excellent presentation summarizing the idea\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.0},{\"vid\":\"2lisQQmWQkY\",\"title\":\"How to use uBlock Origin to protect your online privacy and security | uBlock Origin tutorial 2018\",\"channel\":\"The Hated One\",\"summary\":\"A 2018 tutorial explaining uBlock Origin's advanced user mode, including how to block scripts and use the dynamic filtering settings. It positions the extension as a replacement for tools like uMatrix.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN points newcomers to it as the thing to watch before tackling uBlock Origin's advanced mode and filter syntax.\",\"content_type\":\"tutorial\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"ublock origin advanced mode\",\"categories\":[\"Privacy, surveillance & cybercrime\",\"Web development\"],\"tags\":[\"ublock origin\",\"ad blocking\",\"privacy\",\"script blocking\",\"browser extensions\"],\"quote\":\"Here is a good tutorial on how to use ublock origin in advanced mode.\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.0},{\"vid\":\"2qsmF8HHskg\",\"title\":\"Lisp Editing in the 80s - Interlisp SEdit\",\"channel\":\"thoughtupquick\",\"summary\":\"A short demo of SEdit, the structure editor for Interlisp-D on Xerox Lisp machines in the 1980s, which edits code as trees rather than text.\",\"why_hn\":\"Linked as the clearest view of the legendary structural editor in threads about Lisp environments and structure editing.\",\"content_type\":\"demo\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"structure editors\",\"categories\":[\"Testing, debugging & developer tools\",\"History of computing\",\"Functional programming\"],\"tags\":[\"interlisp\",\"sedit\",\"xerox lisp\",\"structural editing\",\"lisp history\"],\"quote\":\"Dan Ingalls (one of the original authors of Smalltalk) in a 2017 demo of Smalltalk 76\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.0},{\"vid\":\"2vuMzGhc1cg\",\"title\":\"DEBUNKING STARLINK\",\"channel\":\"Common Sense Skeptic\",\"summary\":\"A 43-minute skeptical critique arguing that Starlink fails to live up to its promises, covering satellite lifespan, costs, bandwidth and viability. The creator later added an update about FCC grant requirements.\",\"why_hn\":\"A few commenters recommend it as a skeptical take on Starlink economics, though others see it as dishonest.\",\"content_type\":\"commentary\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"starlink economics\",\"categories\":[\"Space exploration & spaceflight\",\"Networking & internet infrastructure\",\"Tech industry & business models\"],\"tags\":[\"starlink\",\"spacex\",\"satellites\",\"skepticism\",\"elon musk\"],\"quote\":\"watching Common Sense Skeptic’s video, which I recommend\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.0},{\"vid\":\"2wq9x2QcZN0\",\"title\":\"Eric Weinstein: Revolutionary Ideas in Science, Math, and Society | Lex Fridman Podcast #16\",\"channel\":\"Lex Fridman\",\"summary\":\"Lex Fridman interviews mathematician and economist Eric Weinstein about science, mathematics, and society. The conversation ranges across physics, academia, AI and job displacement.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN refers to it for Weinstein's views on advanced math and physics and academia's problems, though some find him a bit kooky.\",\"content_type\":\"podcast\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"science and society\",\"categories\":[\"Tech pioneers & interviews\",\"Fundamental physics\",\"Pure mathematics\"],\"tags\":[\"eric weinstein\",\"physics\",\"academia\",\"ai and jobs\",\"lex fridman\"],\"quote\":\"Eric Weinstein (a bit kooky) explains his view on the trenches of advanced mathematics/physics\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.0},{\"vid\":\"34rdxDgpaaA\",\"title\":\"Well There's Your Problem | Episode 28: Goiânia Incident\",\"channel\":\"Well There's Your Problem Podcast\",\"summary\":\"An episode of the Well There's Your Problem podcast on the 1987 Goiania radiological accident in Brazil, based largely on the IAEA report. It goes through the event day by day.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN points to it as a good, detailed podcast account whenever the Goiania incident or lost radioactive sources come up.\",\"content_type\":\"podcast\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"goiania radiological accident\",\"categories\":[\"Nuclear power & fusion\",\"Documentaries & storytelling\",\"Engineering & making (other)\"],\"tags\":[\"goiania\",\"radiation accident\",\"cesium-137\",\"engineering failures\",\"history\"],\"quote\":\"Goes into detail day by day about the events\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.0},{\"vid\":\"36qZYL5RlgY\",\"title\":\"FreeBSD optimizations used by Netflix serving at 800Gb/s - Drew 