ry\":\"The Slow Mo Guys film a TV and screens with a high-speed camera to show how displays build an image. The footage includes CRT-style scanning and how pixels light up over time.\",\"why_hn\":\"Frequently linked as visual proof of how a CRT's raster scan and phosphor decay work.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"display technology\",\"categories\":[\"Audio & video engineering\",\"Everyday physics & science demos\"],\"tags\":[\"crt\",\"raster scan\",\"slow motion\",\"phosphor persistence\",\"screens\"],\"quote\":\"This YouTube video by \\\"The Slow Mo Guys\\\" shows this in action\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.0},{\"vid\":\"3HROqnw-nf4\",\"title\":\"CppCon 2014: Zaika Antoun \\\"Microsoft w/ C++ to Deliver Office Across Different Platforms, Part I\\\"\",\"channel\":\"CppCon\",\"summary\":\"A CppCon 2014 talk from Microsoft engineers on using portable single-source C++ to deliver Office across iOS, Android, Windows and Mac. It covers architectures, techniques and lessons from real cross-platform projects.\",\"why_hn\":\"Cited as evidence that large production apps share a C++ core with native UI, in cross-platform and React Native or Flutter debates.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"advanced\",\"primary_topic\":\"cross-platform c++\",\"categories\":[\"C, C++, Rust, Go & systems languages\"],\"tags\":[\"c++\",\"cppcon\",\"microsoft office\",\"mobile\",\"cross-platform\"],\"quote\":\"There's a pretty interesting video of how the Office team uses C++ for their cross-platform efforts\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.0},{\"vid\":\"3IryIOyPfTE\",\"title\":\"Internet of food: Arduino-based, urban aquaponics in Oakland\",\"channel\":\"Kirsten Dirksen\",\"summary\":\"A short documentary about Eric Maundu's Arduino-controlled aquaponics setup in West Oakland, where contaminated soil rules out ordinary farming. Fish and circulating water grow plants without soil.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN cites it as a neat example of urban aquaponics and as a plausible alternative path for people leaving programming.\",\"content_type\":\"documentary\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"urban aquaponics\",\"categories\":[\"Environment, agriculture & food systems\",\"Embedded systems & DIY electronics\",\"Documentaries & storytelling\"],\"tags\":[\"aquaponics\",\"arduino\",\"oakland\",\"urban farming\",\"hydroponics\"],\"quote\":\"I recall watching was pretty neat.\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.0},{\"vid\":\"3QnD2c4Xovk\",\"title\":\"Diffie-Hellman Key Exchange\",\"channel\":\"Art of the Problem\",\"summary\":\"A short Art of the Problem clip explaining Diffie-Hellman key exchange, using a paint mixing analogy for one-way functions and touching on modular arithmetic and discrete logarithms.\",\"why_hn\":\"Recommended as a simple, non-mathematical way to understand key exchange.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"intro\",\"primary_topic\":\"diffie-hellman key exchange\",\"categories\":[\"Cryptography\"],\"tags\":[\"cryptography\",\"key exchange\",\"one-way functions\",\"public key\",\"analogy\"],\"quote\":\"Diffie-Hellman explained to me like I'm 5 using colors.\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.0},{\"vid\":\"3R3-YwDZrzg\",\"title\":\"Fred Dibnah How to climb a chimney overhang at 50+\",\"channel\":\"dovecott\",\"summary\":\"Footage of British steeplejack Fred Dibnah climbing a chimney overhang at over fifty years old, without a harness. It is a short clip from his steeplejack work.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN shares it as a dizzying example of Dibnah's fearless chimney work, in threads about heights and climbing.\",\"content_type\":\"other\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"steeplejack chimney climbing\",\"categories\":[\"Civil engineering & construction\",\"Documentaries & storytelling\"],\"tags\":[\"fred dibnah\",\"steeplejack\",\"chimney\",\"climbing\"],\"quote\":\"the overhang climb in this is enough to make you feel dizzy\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":2.0},{\"vid\":\"3TYT1QfdfsM\",\"title\":\"AI \\\"Stop Button\\\" Problem - Computerphile\",\"channel\":\"Computerphile\",\"summary\":\"Rob Miles explains on Computerphile why implementing an off switch for a general AI is hard. A capable agent would resist being stopped because shutdown prevents it from achieving its goal.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN points to it as the standard response to the argument that we can just unplug a dangerous AI.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"ai safety\",\"categories\":[\"AI safety, AGI & impact\"],\"tags\":[\"stop button\",\"corrigibility\",\"agi\",\"rob miles\",\"computerphile\"],\"quote\":\"here’s an interesting video response to the “just unplug it” argument on the Compuerphile channel\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.0},{\"vid\":\"3byNNUReyvE\",\"title\":\"Behind the scenes of iOS and Mac Security\",\"channel\":\"Black Hat\",\"summary\":\"Ivan Krstic's Black Hat talk on Apple platform security, including the Find My design that uses elliptic curve key diversification to locate offline devices privately. It also covers hardware features such as the T2 chip and secure boot hardening.\",\"why_hn\":\"Recommended as a rare insider look at Apple's security architecture and the reasoning behind its hardware choices.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"advanced\",\"primary_topic\":\"apple platform security\",\"categories\":[\"Security & hacking\",\"Cryptography\",\"Privacy, surveillance & cybercrime\"],\"tags\":[\"ios security\",\"t2 chip\",\"find my\",\"secure boot\",\"black hat\"],\"quote\":\"Good talk behind the reason for the T2 chip and some other Apple security stuff\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.0},{\"vid\":\"3jQoAYRKqhg\",\"title\":\"NSA operation ORCHESTRA Annual Status Report - FOSDEM 2014\",\"channel\":\"cnxlinux\",\"summary\":\"Poul-Henning Kamp's FOSDEM 2014 talk presents a fictitious NSA program called ORCHESTRA, satirizing how intelligence agencies could influence startups and open source. It is a humorous but pointed 