gn is costly and hard to fix.\",\"why_hn\":\"Cited in MacBook keyboard and repairability threads for its clear teardown of what a replacement involves.\",\"content_type\":\"commentary\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"macbook keyboard repair\",\"categories\":[\"Repair, teardowns & right to repair\",\"Consumer devices & gadgets\"],\"tags\":[\"louis rossmann\",\"macbook\",\"butterfly keyboard\",\"right to repair\",\"teardown\"],\"quote\":\"Its eye opening seeing a keyboard replacement being performed\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.0},{\"vid\":\"4PHT-zBxKQQ\",\"title\":\"Making Sense of VRChat, the \\\"Metaverse\\\" People Actually Like\",\"channel\":\"People Make Games\",\"summary\":\"People Make Games explores VRChat, the social virtual world that many consider the metaverse people actually like, interviewing users and covering its communities and uncertain future.\",\"why_hn\":\"Recommended as a mini documentary that explains VRChat's culture and contrasts it with Meta's Horizon Worlds.\",\"content_type\":\"documentary\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"vrchat and the metaverse\",\"categories\":[\"VR, AR & spatial computing\",\"Internet culture & memes\",\"Gaming culture & analysis\"],\"tags\":[\"vrchat\",\"metaverse\",\"virtual reality\",\"online communities\",\"social platforms\"],\"quote\":\"There's a great video[1] on VRChat\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.0},{\"vid\":\"4Vw6uF2LdZw\",\"title\":\"The Myth of the Robber Barons with Burt Folsom\",\"channel\":\"Foundation for Economic Education\",\"summary\":\"Hillsdale historian Burt Folsom lectures at a 2011 seminar on the 'robber barons' of the Gilded Age. He argues that figures like Vanderbilt and Rockefeller were market entrepreneurs rather than monopolists.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN people offer it as a free-market counterpoint to the standard robber baron narrative.\",\"content_type\":\"lecture\",\"level\":\"intro\",\"primary_topic\":\"gilded age robber barons\",\"categories\":[\"World history\",\"Microeconomics & behavioral economics\",\"University lectures & courses\"],\"tags\":[\"robber barons\",\"rockefeller\",\"vanderbilt\",\"free market\",\"economic history\"],\"quote\":\"Burton Folsom on the myth of robber barons and the great american entrepreneurs of the 19th century.\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.0},{\"vid\":\"4WwAQqWUkpI\",\"title\":\"Dr. Robert Sapolsky's lecture about Biological Underpinnings of Religiosity\",\"channel\":\"Aprendiendo Juntos\",\"summary\":\"Robert Sapolsky's Stanford lecture on the biological underpinnings of religiosity, from his human behavioral biology course. It covers theories linking religion to stress, and schizotypal traits.\",\"why_hn\":\"Recommended when religion, mental health or psychedelics come up, for Sapolsky's biological framing.\",\"content_type\":\"lecture\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"biology of religion\",\"categories\":[\"University lectures & courses\",\"Neuroscience & the brain\",\"Religion, belief & skepticism\"],\"tags\":[\"robert sapolsky\",\"religiosity\",\"behavioral biology\",\"schizotypy\",\"stanford lecture\"],\"quote\":\"Here's a lecture by Robert Sapolsky where he goes into some theories involving schizotypal individuals\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.0},{\"vid\":\"4_qJptwikRc\",\"title\":\"Dark Matter: The Situation has Changed\",\"channel\":\"Sabine Hossenfelder\",\"summary\":\"Sabine Hossenfelder explains how her opinion on dark matter has shifted, weighing the evidence for and against it and the case for modified gravity. It runs through what dark matter is and why it has not been detected.\",\"why_hn\":\"Recommended as an accessible, curious-undergraduate-level overview of dark matter and its alternatives.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"dark matter\",\"categories\":[\"Cosmology & astrophysics\"],\"tags\":[\"dark matter\",\"modified gravity\",\"astrophysics\",\"cosmology\",\"hossenfelder\"],\"quote\":\"Here’s Sabine Hossenfelde