ries\":[\"Programming language design\",\"Functional programming\",\"Compilers, interpreters & program analysis\"],\"tags\":[\"scala\",\"collections\",\"language critique\",\"subtyping\",\"compiler\"],\"quote\":\"Then I watched this Paul Phillips talk, which convinced me that the problems were deep, not superficial\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.0},{\"vid\":\"4moyKUHApq4\",\"title\":\"A Possible Future of Software Development\",\"channel\":\"Google TechTalks\",\"summary\":\"Sean Parent of Adobe argues that object-oriented frameworks ultimately fail to deliver scalable, high quality software and proposes combining generic and declarative programming instead. It draws on Stepanov's Elements of Programming.\",\"why_hn\":\"Frequently cited for the claim that Photoshop's codebase could shrink dramatically with generic programming.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"advanced\",\"primary_topic\":\"generic programming\",\"categories\":[\"Software architecture & design\",\"C, C++, Rust, Go & systems languages\"],\"tags\":[\"sean parent\",\"generic programming\",\"c++\",\"adobe\",\"software architecture\"],\"quote\":\"Watch this Sean Parent video\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.0},{\"vid\":\"4zG0uecYSMA\",\"title\":\"NeWS: A Networked and Extensible Window System, lecture by James Gosling\",\"channel\":\"Computer History Museum\",\"summary\":\"A 1990 lecture by James Gosling on NeWS, Sun's networked window system in which clients send PostScript programs to the server for execution. It covers the high-level imaging model and compares NeWS with similar systems.\",\"why_hn\":\"Shared in threads on window systems and X11 history as a primary-source talk on why NeWS was technically ahead of X.\",\"content_type\":\"lecture\",\"level\":\"advanced\",\"primary_topic\":\"window system history\",\"categories\":[\"GUI, HCI & interface history\",\"History of computing\",\"Operating systems & kernels\"],\"tags\":[\"news\",\"postscript\",\"james gosling\",\"sun microsystems\",\"x11