 tools\",\"Operating systems & kernels\"],\"tags\":[\"dtrace\",\"bryan cantrill\",\"debugging\",\"observability\",\"solaris\"],\"quote\":\"A video demostration of DTrace, by the creator of DTrace.\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.0},{\"vid\":\"6qD9XElTpCE\",\"title\":\"Quantum Expert Insight:  Peter Shor\",\"channel\":\"Qiskit\",\"summary\":\"Peter Shor tells the story of how he discovered Shor's Algorithm, from his early mathematics days to the quantum factoring breakthrough. It was recorded at MIT at the Physics of Computation conference.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN recommends it as an oral history of the algorithm straight from its inventor.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"shor's algorithm history\",\"categories\":[\"Quantum computing\",\"Tech pioneers & interviews\"],\"tags\":[\"peter shor\",\"quantum computing\",\"factoring\",\"error correction\",\"quantum algorithms\"],\"quote\":\"Shor (yes the one who invented Shor's Algorithm) gave a create 30 min presentation here\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.0},{\"vid\":\"6wZmYMWKLkY\",\"title\":\"Dabble DB demo\",\"channel\":\"krueggen\",\"summary\":\"A short product demo of Dabble DB, a web tool for importing, entering and manipulating structured data with little effort. It was built in Smalltalk and later acquired by Twitter.\",\"why_hn\":\"Used as a reference for an ahead-of-its-time end-user database tool, brought up in threads on Access clones, Smalltalk and data-entry tools.\",\"content_type\":\"demo\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"end-user database tools\",\"categories\":[\"Databases & storage\",\"GUI, HCI & interface history\"],\"tags\":[\"dabble db\",\"smalltalk\",\"spreadsheets\",\"no-code\",\"data entry\"],\"quote\":\"If you haven't heard of DabbleDB, this video is a good introduction\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.0},{\"vid\":\"783ccP__No8\",\"title\":\"GraphQL: The Documentary\",\"channel\":\"CultRepo \",\"summary\":\"A documentary on how GraphQL came to be at Facebook, featuring its co-creators Lee Byron, Dan Schafer and Nick Schrock. It covers the problems it solved and its adoption at companies like Twitter, Airbnb and GitHub.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN recommends it for understanding the original motivation behind GraphQL before judging whether it fits your problem.\",\"content_type\":\"documentary\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"graphql history\",\"categories\":[\"Tech company stories & documentaries\",\"Software architecture & design\",\"Web development\"],\"tags\":[\"graphql\",\"facebook\",\"api design\",\"rest\",\"open source\"],\"quote\":\"Listen to what the developers tell which problems they had to solve when they invented GraphQL.\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.0},{\"vid\":\"7N41TEcjcvM\",\"title\":\"iMUSE Demonstration 2 - Seamless Transitions\",\"channel\":\"Peter Silk (KestrelPi)\",\"summary\":\"A two-minute demonstration of LucasArts' iMUSE adaptive music system in Monkey Island 2. It shows music layers and transitions changing seamlessly as the player moves.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN points to it as the clearest short demo of iMUSE, considered a high point in video game music.\",\"content_type\":\"demo\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"adaptive game music\",\"categories\":[\"Game history & retro gaming\",\"Music theory, synthesis & production\",\"Game programming & engines\"],\"tags\":[\"imuse\",\"monkey island 2\",\"lucasarts\",\"game audio\",\"seamless transitions\"],\"quote\":\"considered a high point in video game music. 1. A video demo\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.0},{\"vid\":\"7PKx3kS7f4A\",\"title\":\"Why Asimov's Laws of Robotics Don't Work - Computerphile\",\"channel\":\"Computerphile\",\"summary\":\"Rob Miles explains for Computerphile why simple rule sets like Asimov's Three Laws cannot make robots and AI safe. Terms like harm and human are too ambiguous to specify precisely.\",\"why_hn\":\"Pointed to in AI safety debates as a short explanation of why encoding human values as simple rul