lections\"],\"tags\":[\"puerto rico\",\"american samoa\",\"citizenship\",\"voting rights\",\"insular cases\"],\"quote\":\"John Oliver has a great, 13-min segment on U.S. territories\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.0},{\"vid\":\"CnMRePtHMZY\",\"title\":\"Thermoelectric cooling: it's not great.\",\"channel\":\"Technology Connections\",\"summary\":\"Technology Connections explains in 33 minutes why thermoelectric (Peltier) cooling is far less efficient than compressor-based refrigeration.\",\"why_hn\":\"It is the standard link whenever a new Peltier or thermoelectric cooling breakthrough is posted.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"thermoelectric cooling\",\"categories\":[\"Power grid, heating & buildings\",\"Everyday physics & science demos\",\"Mechanical & precision engineering\"],\"tags\":[\"peltier\",\"refrigeration\",\"efficiency\",\"heat pumps\",\"technology connections\"],\"quote\":\"they are _massively_ less efficient.\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":2.0},{\"vid\":\"CuD7SCqHB7k\",\"title\":\"RustConf 2017 - Closing Keynote: Safe Systems Software and the Future of Computing by Joe Duffy\",\"channel\":\"Confreaks\",\"summary\":\"Joe Duffy's RustConf 2017 closing keynote on his experience at Microsoft building Midori, an operating system written in a Rust-like safe systems language. He covers the technical and cultural challenges of applying those lessons to Windows.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN repeatedly cites it for Midori lessons: compatibility matters for adoption, and the Windows team stayed sceptical even with Midori running real workloads.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"safe systems programming\",\"categories\":[\"C, C++, Rust, Go & systems languages\",\"Operating systems & kernels\",\"Security & hacking\"],\"tags\":[\"midori\",\"rust\",\"operating systems\",\"microsoft\",\"memory safety\"],\"quote\":\"I summarized this excellent talk here [1], but one of the main points is that compatibility with existing systems is important for adoption.\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.0},{\"vid\":\"CvRAqR2pAgw\",\"title\":\"Money creation in the modern economy - Quarterly Bulletin\",\"channel\":\"Bank of England\",\"summary\":\"A short Bank of England video accompanying its 2014 Quarterly Bulletin article on money creation. It explains that most money is bank deposits and that commercial banks create new money by making loans, which simultaneously create matching deposits.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN people use it as an authoritative, plain-English source from a central bank that loans create deposits, rather than banks lending out saved money.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"intro\",\"primary_topic\":\"money creation\",\"categories\":[\"Macroeconomics & financial crises\"],\"tags\":[\"bank of england\",\"fractional reserve banking\",\"bank loans\",\"deposits\",\"monetary economics\"],\"quote\":\"Some of the content is in this short video\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.0},{\"vid\":\"Cwas_7H5KUs\",\"title\":\"J.S.Bach \\\"The Goldberg Variations\\\" [ Glenn Gould ] (1955)\",\"channel\":\"BATACHAN DESU\",\"summary\":\"Glenn Gould's 1955 recording of Bach's Goldberg Variations, uploaded as a continuous performance of about 39 minutes.\",\"why_hn\":\"Recommended as the best-known and most famous recording of the Goldberg Variations.\",\"content_type\":\"music\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"bach goldberg variations\",\"categories\":[\"Music performance & songs\"],\"tags\":[\"bach\",\"glenn gould\",\"goldberg variations\",\"classical piano\",\"1955 recording\"],\"quote\":\"Glenn Gould's 1955 recording is perhaps the best known recording of this work\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.0},{\"vid\":\"CxHa5KaMBcM\",\"title\":\"5 Hours of The Shipping Forecast on BBC Radio 4!\",\"channel\":\"icannotgetafreename\",\"summary\":\"Five hours of the late-night BBC Radio 4 Shipping Forecast, uploaded to mark its 150th anniversary. It can be used as sleep au