    ",{\"vid\":\"EH6vE97qIP4\",\"title\":\"1. Introduction for 15.S12 Blockchain and Money, Fall 2018\",\"channel\":\"MIT OpenCourseWare\",\"summary\":\"The opening lecture of MIT's Blockchain and Money course taught by Gary Gensler, covering the course plan, the history of failed digital currencies, cryptography and what a blockchain is.\",\"why_hn\":\"Recommended as a solid, level-headed academic introduction to blockchain, often noted because Gensler later led the SEC.\",\"content_type\":\"lecture\",\"level\":\"intro\",\"primary_topic\":\"blockchain and money\",\"categories\":[\"Cryptography\",\"University lectures & courses\",\"Macroeconomics & financial crises\"],\"tags\":[\"blockchain\",\"bitcoin\",\"mit opencourseware\",\"gary gensler\",\"cryptocurrency\"],\"quote\":\"I've been enjoying a playlist of blockchain lectures by Gary Gensler\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.0},{\"vid\":\"EL7Au1tzNxE\",\"title\":\"Vibe coding complex changes in Rust\",\"channel\":\"Jon Gjengset\",\"summary\":\"Jon Gjengset spends about three hours livecoding complex changes in a Rust codebase with agentic AI tools, testing his hypothesis that AI is weak at non-pattern work. He documents where Claude Code helps and where it struggles.\",\"why_hn\":\"Pointed to as a non-promotional, realistic long session of an experienced engineer working with AI on non-trivial code.\",\"content_type\":\"demo\",\"level\":\"advanced\",\"primary_topic\":\"ai-assisted programming\",\"categories\":[\"LLMs & generative AI\",\"C, C++, Rust, Go & systems languages\",\"Software practice, open source & careers\"],\"tags\":[\"vibe coding\",\"claude code\",\"rust\",\"agentic ai\",\"livecoding\"],\"quote\":\"I found this one and sat down and watched the whole three hours.\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.0},{\"vid\":\"EP9F-AZezCU\",\"title\":\"[Highlight] StarCraft Remastered Rant\",\"channel\":\"Day9TV\",\"summary\":\"Day9 gives a passionate first look at what his StarCraft: Brood War Remastered series will teach. He argues Brood War is primarily a real-time game and only secondarily a strategy game, making the commander fantasy a matter of mechanics.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN uses it to argue that mechanical difficulty and limited attention are integral to RTS strategy, especially in StarCraft AI threads.\",\"content_type\":\"commentary\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"starcraft rts design\",\"categories\":[\"Game design\",\"Gaming culture & analysis\"],\"tags\":[\"starcraft\",\"brood war\",\"day9\",\"rts\",\"game design\",\"micro\"],\"quote\":\"day[9] (ex Broodwar pro, current caster of many games) probably makes the argument better than I can here\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.0},{\"vid\":\"EcKxaq1FTac\",\"title\":\"The KGB, the Computer, and Me (Complete)\",\"channel\":\"GBPPR2\",\"summary\":\"The 1990 NOVA documentary follows astronomer Clifford Stoll as he tracks a hacker through military and research computer networks, a story that involved the CIA and KGB. It is based on The Cuckoo's Egg.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN lists it among favorite nerdy documentaries and enjoys hearing Stoll tell the story himself.\",\"content_type\":\"documentary\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"early computer espionage\",\"categories\":[\"Security & hacking\",\"History of computing\",\"Privacy, surveillance & cybercrime\"],\"tags\":[\"cliff stoll\",\"cuckoo's egg\",\"kgb\",\"nova\",\"hacking history\"],\"quote\":\"It was really great, getting to hear it from Mr. Stoll's mouth directly.\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.0},{\"vid\":\"EeYvFl7li9E\",\"title\":\"Ryan Dahl: Node JS\",\"channel\":\"JSConf\",\"summary\":\"Ryan Dahl's JSConf EU talk introducing Node.js to the world. He explains the motivation for event-driven, non-blocking I/O, with JavaScript chosen mainly for its asynchronous nature.\",\"why_hn\":\"Cited as the primary source for why Node exists and why JavaScript was chosen, in debates about async models and language choice.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"nodejs origins\",\"categories\":[\"Web development\",\"Tech pioneers & interviews\"],\"tags\":[\"node.js\",\"event loop\",\"async io\",\"javascript\",\"ryan dahl\"],\"quote\":\"it's kind of refreshing to see the original node.js presentation, where using javascript is sort of a side-note\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.0},{\"vid\":\"EfjdOc41g0s\",\"title\":\"The benefits of deploying IPv6 only\",\"channel\":\"NANOG\",\"summary\":\"A NANOG 64 panel with speakers from Comcast, APNIC, T-Mobile and Facebook on deploying IPv6-only networks, including performance data showing IPv6 outperforming NAT-ed IPv4.\",\"why_hn\":\"Cited as real operator data that IPv6 is faster than IPv4 and that large networks are already going IPv6-only.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"ipv6 deployment\",\"categories\":[\"Networking & internet infrastructure\"],\"tags\":[\"ipv6\",\"nanog\",\"networking\",\"ipv4 depletion\",\"nat\"],\"quote\":\"Watch Paul Saab from Facebook talk about how much better IPv6 performs at NANOG 64\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":2.0},{\"vid\":\"EgMqhEMhVV8\",\"title\":\"Game Theory: How PewDiePie Conquered YouTube\",\"channel\":\"The Game Theorists\",\"summary\":\"The Game Theorists analyze how PewDiePie rose to become the most subscribed channel on YouTube. The video looks at why let's plays and gaming channels thrive on the platform.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN commenters cite it as an analysis of PewDiePie's popularity and of how YouTube's recommendations favored gaming content.\",\"content_type\":\"commentary\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"youtube creator economy\",\"categories\":[\"Internet culture & memes\",\"Gaming culture & analysis\",\"Product, marketing & sales\"],\"tags\":[\"pewdiepie\",\"let's play\",\"youtube algorithm\",\"gaming channels\",\"game theory\"],\"quote\":\"Here's a video with some interesting theories about how PewDiePie, and other gaming channels, are so popular\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.0},{\"vid\":\"Eg_ToU7m1MI\",\"title\":\"Alan Kay: A powerful idea about teaching ideas\",\"channel\":\"TED\",\"summary\":\"Alan Kay's TED talk on teaching ideas, in which he argues the world is not what it seems and shows children learning through programming and building their own lessons with Etoys/Squeak.\",\"why_hn\":\"Recommended as a condensed version of Kay's ideas on education and computing, showing kids using software to explore physics and robotics.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"computing and education\",\"categories\":[\"Education & learning\",\"Tech pioneers & interviews\",\"GUI, HCI & interface history\"],\"tags\":[\"alan kay\",\"etoys\",\"squeak\",\"children\",\"learning by doing\"],\"quote\":\"You'll see kids using the software to explore robotics and do physics of gravitation.\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.0},{\"vid\":\"EkpQAGQiv4Q\",\"title\":\"The Wright Brothers DID Invent the Airplane\",\"channel\":\"Greg's Airplanes and Automobiles\",\"summary\":\"A long rebuttal arguing that the Wright Brothers truly invented the airplane, responding to other YouTubers who credit others. It walks through the engineering breakthroughs the Wrights achieved, such as control and wind tunnel work.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN commenters use it as a well-researched account of what the Wrights actually solved, in threads on airplane physics and invention credit.\",\"content_type\":\"documentary\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"history of aviation\",\"categories\":[\"Aviation & aerospace engineering\",\"World history\"],\"tags\":[\"wright brothers\",\"first flight\",\"aeronautics\",\"invention credit\",\"wind tunnel\"],\"quote\":\"This video has a nice delineation of the collection of breakthroughs needed\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.0},{\"vid\":\"Em7nqDqQ8oM\",\"title\":\"Strong Towns | Charles Marohn | Talks at Google\",\"channel\":\"Talks at Google\",\"summary\":\"Charles Marohn of Strong Towns presents, in a Talks at Google session, the ideas from his book on why many North American towns struggle financially despite decades of growth. He argues for incremental, bottom-up city building as a path to local prosperity.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN commenters link it in housing and urbanism threads as a clear explanation of unsustainable car-oriented development and fragile systems.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"urban planning and municipal finance\",\"categories\":[\"Transit, cities & urban planning\",\"Startups & entrepreneurship\"],\"tags\":[\"strong towns\",\"charles marohn\",\"incremental development\",\"suburban finance\",\"housing\"],\"quote\":\"It has a great explanation of the difference between complex and complicated\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.0},{\"vid\":\"EpRrD58Ah3Q\",\"title\":\"Evidence-Based Weight Loss: Live Presentation\",\"channel\":\"NutritionFacts.org\",\"summary\":\"Dr. Michael Greger gives a live presentation on evidence-based weight loss, previewing his book How Not to Diet. He focuses on foods that aid weight loss while also supporting health and longevity.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN commenters share it as a helpful lecture on plant-based weight loss and which foods to experiment with.\",\"content_type\":\"lecture\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"weight loss nutrition\",\"categories\":[\"Nutrition & diet science\",\"Medicine & infectious disease\"],\"tags\":[\"plant-based diet\",\"satiety\",\"obesity\",\"michael greger\",\"diet\"],\"quote\":\"I also find this lecture helpful for thinking about foods to experiment with\",\"recommenders\":1,\"score\":2.0},{\"vid\":\"EuELwq2ThJE\",\"title\":\"Don't Make Me Click\",\"channel\":\"Google TechTalks\",\"summary\":\"A Google Tech Talk arguing that the best interface requires the fewest clicks and choices, with Google search, Facebook, the iPod and Firefox as examples. It shows how minimizing interaction makes interfaces easier to learn.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN commenters recommend it as a companion to Steve Krug's usability advice and as a talk on minimal interface design.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"intro\",\"primary_topic\":\"interface design\",\"categories\":[\"UX & UI design\"],\"tags\":[\"usability\",\"minimal interaction\",\"web design\",\"ux\",\"google tech talks\"],\"quote\":\"Read Don't Make Me Think! by Steve Krug. Also watch this talk titled\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.0},{\"vid\":\"Ev373c7wSRg\",\"title\":\"When Wokes and Racists Actually Agree on Everything\",\"channel\":\"Ryan Long\",\"summary\":\"A short comedy skit by Ryan Long satirizing how woke activists and racists end up agreeing on many things.\",\"why_hn\":\"Posted as relevant satire in threads on wokeness and identity politics, with some saying it is barely an exaggeration.\",\"content_type\":\"comedy\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"political satire\",\"categories\":[\"Satire & parody\",\"Social issues & culture\"],\"tags\":[\"ryan long\",\"woke\",\"satire\",\"skit\",\"identity politics\"],\"quote\":null,\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.0},{\"vid\":\"F-yDKeya4SU\",\"title\":\"America Was Wrong About Ethanol - Study Shows\",\"channel\":\"Engineering Explained\",\"summary\":\"Engineering Explained examines new research suggesting corn ethanol in US gasoline may emit as much or more carbon than gasoline. It covers the Renewable Fuel Standard and why ethanol was assumed to be a green fuel.\",\"why_hn\":\"Cited as an accessible summary of evidence that corn ethanol is no better than gasoline for emissions.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"corn ethanol emissions\",\"categories\":[\"Climate policy, solutions & debate\",\"Cars, EVs & motorcycles\",\"Earth & energy (other)\"],\"tags\":[\"ethanol\",\"renewable fuel standard\",\"carbon emissions\",\"biofuels\",\"gasoline\"],\"quote\":\"Corn-based ethanol is at best as bad a carbon emitter as gasoline, and it's most likely worse.\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.0},{\"vid\":\"F04dGK1_wYA\",\"title\":\"Fred Dibnah laddering a chimney (Part 1)\",\"channel\":\"Matibeos\",\"summary\":\"Fred Dibnah, the English steeplejack, shows how ladders are fixed up the outside of a tall brick mill chimney. The footage was filmed in the mid-1990s and is part one of two.\",\"why_hn\":\"People point to it as a vivid explanation of how industrial chimneys were climbed for inspection and repair.\",\"content_type\":\"documentary\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"steeplejack chimney climbing\",\"categories\":[\"Civil engineering & construction\",\"Documentaries & storytelling\"],\"tags\":[\"fred dibnah\",\"chimney\",\"steeplejack\",\"industrial heritage\",\"ladders\"],\"quote\":\"there is a great series showing how industrial chimneys made of brick were climbed for inspection and repair.\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.0},{\"vid\":\"F1Hq8eVOMHs\",\"title\":\"Is Meat Really that Bad?\",\"channel\":\"Kurzgesagt – In a Nutshell\",\"summary\":\"A Kurzgesagt animated explainer on the climate and environmental cost of meat. It covers how beef drives deforestation and emissions, and how this compares with plant-based foods.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN commenters cite it as a clear, well-sourced summary of why meat, especially beef, has such a large environmental footprint.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"environmental impact of meat\",\"categories\":[\"Environment, agriculture & food systems\",\"Climate science & climate change\",\"Nutrition & diet science\"],\"tags\":[\"climate change\",\"meat\",\"deforestation\",\"food emissions\",\"kurzgesagt\"],\"quote\":\"Kurzgesagt just did a great video on the subject\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.0},{\"vid\":\"F8JCh0owT4w\",\"title\":\"Tractor Hacking: The Farmers Breaking Big Tech's Repair Monopoly\",\"channel\":\"Motherboard\",\"summary\":\"A Motherboard documentary episode from Nebraska about farmers and mechanics fighting manufacturers like John Deere over access to the diagnostic software needed to repair modern tractors. It shows how software locks have taken away farmers' traditional self-reliance.\",\"why_hn\":\"Offered as a concrete, human example in right-to-repair discussions of how software lock-in affects expensive equipment.\",\"content_type\":\"documentary\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"right to repair\",\"categories\":[\"Repair, teardowns & right to repair\",\"Environment, agriculture & food systems\",\"Documentaries & storytelling\"],\"tags\":[\"john deere\",\"tractors\",\"farming\",\"diagnostic software\",\"repair monopoly\"],\"quote\":\"It's worth a look.\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":2.0},{\"vid\":\"FBsP-bmDLOo\",\"title\":\"All you need to know to understand 5G\",\"channel\":\"Sabine Hossenfelder\",\"summary\":\"Physicist Sabine Hossenfelder explains how 5G works and examines the health concerns around millimeter wave radiation. She reviews the scientific evidence and the open letters from scientists.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN recommends it as an even-handed physicist's take for 5G skeptics, noting it is probably safe but under-studied.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"5g health risks\",\"categories\":[\"Networking & internet infrastructure\",\"Fundamental physics\",\"Medicine & infectious disease\"],\"tags\":[\"5g\",\"millimeter wave\",\"radiation\",\"health\",\"physics\"],\"quote\":\"this is an even-handed (reasonably well-informed) take on the matter from physicist Sabine Hossenfelder\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.0},{\"vid\":\"FH2WeWgcSMk\",\"title\":\"Part One: The Evergreen Equity Council\",\"channel\":\"Michael Nayna\",\"summary\":\"The first of three short films by Mike Nayna about Bret Weinstein and Heather Heying's experience at Evergreen State College, focusing on the Equity Council and the controversy around it.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN commenters cite the series as a documentary on the Evergreen controversy and as evidence in arguments about ideology and campus culture.\",\"content_type\":\"documentary\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"evergreen college controversy\",\"categories\":[\"Free speech, censorship & civil liberties\",\"Social issues & culture\",\"Documentaries & storytelling\"],\"tags\":[\"evergreen state college\",\"bret weinstein\",\"campus politics\",\"free speech\",\"documentary\"],\"quote\":\"the great, 3-part, documentary[3] by Mike Nayna\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.0},{\"vid\":\"FV0DXNB94NE\",\"title\":\"\\\"Make the Back-End Team Jealous: Elm in Production\\\" by Richard Feldman\",\"channel\":\"Strange Loop Conference\",\"summary\":\"Richard Feldman describes introducing Elm into a mixed React and jQuery front-end in production, and why the result was reliable, clean and fast enough to make the back-end team jealous.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN people recommend it as a quick way to get a sense of what Elm does and what adopting it incrementally looks like.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"elm in production\",\"categories\":[\"Functional programming\",\"Web development\"],\"tags\":[\"elm\",\"functional programming\",\"front-end\",\"react migration\",\"strange loop\"],\"quote\":\"Watch this conference to get a sense of what Elm does.\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.0},{\"vid\":\"FV8n_E_6Tpc\",\"title\":\"Make love, not porn (Adult content) | Cindy Gallop\",\"channel\":\"TED\",\"summary\":\"Cindy Gallop gives a 4-minute TED2009 talk arguing hardcore pornography has distorted how young men think about sex. She introduces her website MakeLoveNotPorn as a response.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN people share it as a short, frank talk about porn versus real-life sex expectations.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"pornography and sex education\",\"categories\":[\"Social issues & culture\",\"Ideas & learning (other)\"],\"tags\":[\"ted\",\"cindy gallop\",\"porn\",\"sex education\",\"makelovenotporn\"],\"quote\":\"she raises some good points so I recommend the video (it's 4 minutes).\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.0},{\"vid\":\"FegjLbCnoBw\",\"title\":\"XFS: Recent and Future Adventures in Filesystem Scalability - Dave Chinner\",\"channel\":\"Linux.conf.au 2012 -- Ballarat, Australia\",\"summary\":\"Dave Chinner's linux.conf.au 2012 talk on XFS scalability, covering pain points with large numbers of files and complex metadata, and the work to fix XFS metadata performance.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN recommends it as the definitive explanation of XFS metadata performance fixes and how XFS was developed and made robust on Linux.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"advanced\",\"primary_topic\":\"xfs filesystem scalability\",\"categories\":[\"Databases & storage\",\"Linux & open-source ecosystems\",\"Operating systems & kernels\"],\"tags\":[\"xfs\",\"filesystems\",\"linux kernel\",\"metadata performance\",\"dave chinner\"],\"quote\":\"Please check this talk from Dave Chinner, where he explains how XFS was developed and ported to Linux\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.0},{\"vid\":\"FlQYU3m1e80\",\"title\":\"Is It Really Impossible To Cool A Datacenter In Space?\",\"channel\":\"Scott Manley\",\"summary\":\"Scott Manley explains the thermal balance of spacecraft and how a satellite could be configured to radiate away the heat from datacenter-scale computing in space. His rough numbers suggest it is feasible.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN points to it as a convincing energy-budget analysis in debates over space datacenters, while debating its assumptions.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"space datacenter cooling\",\"categories\":[\"Space exploration & spaceflight\",\"Fundamental physics\",\"Computer architecture & CPUs\"],\"tags\":[\"thermal radiation\",\"starlink\",\"spacecraft thermal\",\"scott manley\",\"orbital datacenter\"],\"quote\":\"the Scott Manley video alas has sort of convinced me this is pretty feasible, that the energy budget is quite doable.\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.0},{\"vid\":\"FquNpWdf9vg\",\"title\":\"The Computer Chronicles - Hypercard (1987)\",\"channel\":\"The Computer Chronicles\",\"summary\":\"A 1987 episode of The Computer Chronicles on Apple's HyperCard, showing users building their own applications. Gary Kildall appears and Bill Atkinson discusses the program, with credit given to earlier influences.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN points to it as a period view of HyperCard and a source for its history and influences.\",\"content_type\":\"documentary\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"hypercard history\",\"categories\":[\"GUI, HCI & interface history\",\"History of computing\",\"Tech company stories & documentaries\"],\"tags\":[\"hypercard\",\"bill atkinson\",\"gary kildall\",\"apple\",\"computer history\"],\"quote\":\"Years ago I stumbled on this (wonderfully dorky) episode of Computer Chronicles, that focuses on HyperCard\",\"recommenders\":1,\"score\":2.0},{\"vid\":\"FyKRubB5N60\",\"title\":\"Why Sony's Beta Videotape System Failed--and failed hard (Part 1)\",\"channel\":\"Technology Connections\",\"summary\":\"Part one of Technology Connections' account of the VHS versus Betamax format war. It argues Sony was caught off guard by JVC's cheaper, more practical VHS system.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN recommends it as a detailed, accurate explanation of why Betamax lost, and cites it in debates over whether VHS was actually the worse format.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"betamax vs vhs format war\",\"categories\":[\"Audio & video engineering\",\"Tech industry & business models\",\"History of computing\"],\"tags\":[\"betamax\",\"vhs\",\"format war\",\"videotape\",\"consumer electronics\"],\"quote\":\"Here's a very good video going into details\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.0},{\"vid\":\"FzF1KySHmUA\",\"title\":\"For the undying 9/11 MORONIC JET FUEL ARGUMENT\",\"channel\":\"purgatoryironworks\",\"summary\":\"A short video from a blacksmith, who heats and bends steel to rebut the claim that jet fuel could not weaken the steel in the World Trade Center. It is delivered with a lot of attitude.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN commenters use it as a quick, hands-on demonstration that steel loses strength well below its melting point.\",\"content_type\":\"demo\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"steel strength at fire temperatures\",\"categories\":[\"Woodworking, metalworking & workshop skills\",\"Media, journalism & propaganda\",\"Materials science\"],\"tags\":[\"blacksmithing\",\"jet fuel\",\"9/11\",\"steel\",\"conspiracy debunking\"],\"quote\":\"watch this excellent and short video from a blacksmith\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.0},{\"vid\":\"FzRP1qdwPKw\",\"title\":\"How To Contact The Voyager 2 Probe (PART 1)\",\"channel\":\"EEVdiscover\",\"summary\":\"Dave Jones of EEVblog and Richard Stephenson tour the 70m DSS43 dish at the Canberra Deep Space Communication Complex and explain how NASA talks to Voyager 2. It covers the transmitters, receivers and tracking involved.\",\"why_hn\":\"Recommended in Voyager threads as the best look at how operators actually contact the probe.\",\"content_type\":\"tutorial\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"deep space communications\",\"categories\":[\"Space exploration & spaceflight\",\"Electronics & circuit design\"],\"tags\":[\"voyager 2\",\"deep space network\",\"canberra\",\"radio dish\",\"nasa\"],\"quote\":\"Dave Jones of EEVBlog has a nice series of videos talking to Richard Stephenson, Operations Supervisor at the DSN's Canberra site.\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.0},{\"vid\":\"Fzmm87oVQ6c\",\"title\":\"My personal fight against the modern laptop\",\"channel\":\"linux conf au 2017 - Hobart, Australia\",\"summary\":\"Hamish Coleman describes reverse engineering the keyboard controller in a Thinkpad and reflashing it with custom firmware. He covers how Lenovo secures its firmware, and his ongoing work on the protocol between the BIOS and the vendor flash tool.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN people cite it as an approachable, hands-on introduction to hardware and firmware reverse engineering, and as the author's own account of the Thinkpad keyboard patch effort.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"advanced\",\"primary_topic\":\"firmware reverse engineering\",\"categories\":[\"Security & hacking\",\"Embedded systems & DIY electronics\",\"Consumer devices & gadgets\"],\"tags\":[\"thinkpad\",\"reverse engineering\",\"embedded controller\",\"firmware\",\"bios\"],\"quote\":\"Here's the presentation by the author himself at linux.conf.au\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.0},{\"vid\":\"G-lN8vWm3m0\",\"title\":\"Try this bizarre audio illusion! 👁️👂😮 - BBC\",\"channel\":\"BBC\",\"summary\":\"A BBC Horizon clip demonstrating the McGurk effect, where the same audio sounds like different syllables depending on the mouth movements you see. It shows that people integrate visual speech information into what they hear.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN uses it as the standard demonstration that the brain reinterprets perception, in threads on speech, AI audio and illusions.\",\"content_type\":\"demo\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"mcgurk effect\",\"categories\":[\"Neuroscience & the brain\",\"Magic, puzzles & curiosities\",\"Language & linguistics\"],\"tags\":[\"perception\",\"auditory illusion\",\"speech\",\"lip reading\",\"neuroscience\"],\"quote\":\"The most compelling illustration I've seen of this is the McGurk Affect[1].\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.0},{\"vid\":\"G5B1mIfQuo4\",\"title\":\"YMS: Kimba the White Lion\",\"channel\":\"YMS\",\"summary\":\"A roughly two and a half hour YMS video on Kimba the White Lion that investigates the claim that Disney's The Lion King copied it.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN recommends it as the thorough investigation of the Kimba and Lion King controversy, and as a quality benchmark for the reviewer.\",\"content_type\":\"commentary\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"kimba and the lion king\",\"categories\"