version using VQ compression\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.0},{\"vid\":\"Ot4qdCs54ZE\",\"title\":\"How The Dutch Economy Shows We Can't Reduce Wealth Inequality With Taxes | Economics Explained\",\"channel\":\"Economics Explained\",\"summary\":\"An Economics Explained video arguing that the Netherlands shows taxes alone can't reduce wealth inequality. It distinguishes income inequality from wealth inequality and discusses the Gini index.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN uses it to explain the difference between income and wealth inequality, though some pair it with a rebuttal.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"intro\",\"primary_topic\":\"wealth inequality\",\"categories\":[\"Labor, work & inequality\",\"Macroeconomics & financial crises\"],\"tags\":[\"netherlands\",\"gini coefficient\",\"income inequality\",\"taxation\",\"economics\"],\"quote\":\"This video gives a good explanation about their difference\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.0},{\"vid\":\"OyBNmecVtdU\",\"title\":\"Eisenhower Farewell Address (Best Quality) - 'Military Industrial Complex' WARNING\",\"channel\":\"Ewafa\",\"summary\":\"A high-quality recording of President Eisenhower's January 1961 farewell address, including his warning about the unwarranted influence of the military-industrial complex. The uploader marks the key passage at 8:41.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN commenters link it as the primary source for the phrase 'military-industrial complex' and urge people to hear the full speech rather than the soundbite.\",\"content_type\":\"other\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"military-industrial complex\",\"categories\":[\"US politics & elections\",\"Military history & warfare\",\"World history\"],\"tags\":[\"eisenhower\",\"farewell address\",\"1961\",\"defense spending\",\"us politics\"],\"quote\":\"Eisenhower's 1961 Farewell Address is misinterpreted by many and totally forgotten by others. Please listen\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.0},{\"vid\":\"P1IcaBn3ej0\",\"title\":\"Enhancing Photorealism Enhancement\",\"channel\":\"ISL and Collaborators\",\"summary\":\"A video presenting an Intel research paper on enhancing the photorealism of synthetic images. A convolutional network uses rendering intermediates, shown on GTA V footage that comes out looking like real street scenes.\",\"why_hn\":\"Used as a go-to example of neural networks enhancing game rendering, referenced in later AI-graphics discussions.\",\"content_type\":\"demo\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"neural photorealism enhancement\",\"categories\":[\"Computer graphics & rendering\",\"Machine learning & deep learning\",\"LLMs & generative AI\"],\"tags\":[\"neural rendering\",\"gan\",\"gta v\",\"computer graphics\",\"intel\"],\"quote\":\"The video linked of applying a neural net to GTAV for photorealism is really impressive if you haven't seen it.\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.0},{\"vid\":\"PC2JOQ7z5L0\",\"title\":\"What Happens After the Universe Ends?\",\"channel\":\"PBS Space Time\",\"summary\":\"PBS Space Time explains Roger Penrose's conformal cyclic cosmology, in which the far future of our universe becomes the big bang of the next. It explores what could come after the universe ends.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN recommends it as a clearer explanation of Penrose's cyclic cosmology than comment threads can give.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"cosmology\",\"categories\":[\"Cosmology & astrophysics\"],\"tags\":[\"penrose\",\"conformal cyclic cosmology\",\"heat death\",\"big bang\",\"physics\"],\"quote\":\"It's explained in this PBS Space Time episode much better\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.0},{\"vid\":\"PDL_pIPScSI\",\"title\":\"Minuteman III attacks Kwajalein\",\"channel\":\"Eureka\",\"summary\":\"Footage of a Minuteman III ICBM test launch and its reentry vehicles striking the Kwajalein atoll target area. It shows the missile climbing through clouds and the warheads descending.\",\"why_hn\":\"Linked as unusually clear real footage of ICBM reentries and impacts whenever missile tests or the Marshall Islands come up.\",\"content_type\":\"demo\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"icbm tests\",\"categories\":[\"Military history & warfare\"],\"tags\":[\"minuteman iii\",\"kwajalein\",\"reentry vehicles\",\"nuclear deterrent\",\"missile test\"],\"quote\":\"It has some of the clearest footage of the actual reentries and impacts\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.0},{\"vid\":\"PHiyQID7SBs\",\"title\":\"The Equation That Explains (Nearly) Everything!\",\"channel\":\"PBS Space Time\",\"summary\":\"PBS Space Time explains the Standard Model Lagrangian, the single equation encapsulating the particle physics theory, and visualizes what its terms mean.\",\"why_hn\":\"Recommended as a good visual walkthrough of the Standard Model equation for people who want to understand its terms.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"standard model of particle physics\",\"categories\":[\"Quantum physics\",\"Fundamental physics\"],\"tags\":[\"standard model\",\"lagrangian\",\"particle physics\",\"symmetry\",\"quantum field theory\"],\"quote\":\"PBS Spacetime has a very good video[0] that helps visualize what's going on in the equation, recent too!\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.0}",
    ",{\"vid\":\"PTUY16CkS-k\",\"title\":\"Quantitative Easing Explained\",\"channel\":\"malekanoms\",\"summary\":\"An animated xtranormal explainer on quantitative easing, what the Federal Reserve was doing and how things got there. It was made by Omid Malekan.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN pointed to it in 2011 as a nice, tongue-in-cheek explanation of quantitative easing.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"intro\",\"primary_topic\":\"quantitative easing\",\"categories\":[\"Macroeconomics & financial crises\"],\"tags\":[\"federal reserve\",\"monetary policy\",\"bernanke\",\"xtranormal\",\"money creation\"],\"quote\":\"QE is Quantitative Easing which is nicely explained in this great xtranormal video\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.0},{\"vid\":\"PZRI1IfStY0\",\"title\":\"Floating Point Numbers - Computerphile\",\"channel\":\"Computerphile\",\"summary\":\"Tom Scott explains for Computerphile how floating point numbers work, why moving the binary point is fast, and why it handles money badly.\",\"why_hn\":\"Recommended as a simple, fun explanation of why floating point gives odd errors like 0.1 + 0.2.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"intro\",\"primary_topic\":\"floating point numbers\",\"categories\":[\"Computer architecture & CPUs\",\"Information theory & signal processing\"],\"tags\":[\"floating point\",\"ieee 754\",\"binary\",\"currency\",\"computerphile\"],\"quote\":\"Tom Scott's fun and simple take on Floating Points is a good video explaining why such weird errors happen\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.0},{\"vid\":\"PaKIZ7gJlRU\",\"title\":\"Linus Torvalds says GPL v3 violates everything that GPLv2 stood for\",\"channel\":\"TFiR\",\"summary\":\"A short TFiR clip of Linus Torvalds explaining why he thinks GPLv3 violates what GPLv2 stood for. He describes why he chose GPLv2 for kernel development and his view of the FSF's approach.\",\"why_hn\":\"Cited again and again in GPL licensing debates as the primary source for Linus's objections to GPLv3.\",\"