orous, entertaining example of interface design review and notes the author later became head of design at MuseScore.\",\"content_type\":\"commentary\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"software interface design\",\"categories\":[\"UX & UI design\",\"Music theory, synthesis & production\"],\"tags\":[\"ux review\",\"music notation\",\"dorico\",\"user testing\",\"interface design\"],\"quote\":\"In another video on Dorico [0], he did user testing. So he's not just pulling things out his ass.\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.0},{\"vid\":\"S-VAL7Epn3o\",\"title\":\"How Command & Conquer: Tiberian Sun Solved Pathfinding | War Stories | Ars Technica\",\"channel\":\"Ars Technica\",\"summary\":\"Westwood Studios co-founder Louis Castle talks about how pathfinding was solved in Command & Conquer: Tiberian Sun, in an Ars Technica War Stories episode. It also touches on other challenges in Westwood's RTS games.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN commenters recommend it as an accessible, non-technical look at real game pathfinding problems from a developer who built them.\",\"content_type\":\"interview\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"game pathfinding\",\"categories\":[\"Game programming & engines\",\"Game history & retro gaming\"],\"tags\":[\"pathfinding\",\"rts\",\"westwood studios\",\"command & conquer\",\"game development\"],\"quote\":\"Ars Technica had a series of 10 minute videos where they interviewed developers about technical challenges.\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.0},{\"vid\":\"S0dSm_ClcSw\",\"title\":\"This high-speed rail project is a warning for the US\",\"channel\":\"Vox\",\"summary\":\"A Vox explainer on why California's high-speed rail project is years late and far over budget, with only a few concrete structures built by 2022. It covers the political, legal and routing challenges behind the delays.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN uses it as a high-level intro to how US megaprojects get stalled by regulation, litigation and local demands.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\