ong\",\"second law\",\"british humor\"],\"quote\":\"The classic Flanders and Swann explanation\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.0},{\"vid\":\"Vrq2akzdFq8\",\"title\":\"Tested: Magic Leap One Augmented Reality Review!\",\"channel\":\"Adam Savage’s Tested\",\"summary\":\"Adam Savage's Tested spends a week with the Magic Leap One developer kit. They dig into the hardware, display technology, user experience and launch apps.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN recommends it as an in-depth independent review that tempers expectations and adds technical detail beyond Magic Leap's own materials.\",\"content_type\":\"other\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"magic leap one review\",\"categories\":[\"VR, AR & spatial computing\",\"Consumer devices & gadgets\"],\"tags\":[\"magic leap\",\"augmented reality\",\"headset review\",\"tested\",\"display tech\"],\"quote\":\"I'd recommend you check out the [Tested review][1]\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":2.0},{\"vid\":\"VxINoKFm-S4\",\"title\":\"\\\"A Little Taste of Dependent Types\\\" by David Christiansen\",\"channel\":\"Strange Loop Conference\",\"summary\":\"David Christiansen gives a Strange Loop 2018 introduction to dependent types, where one language serves for both compile-time and run-time code and programs unite with proofs. It draws on his book The Little Typer.\",\"why_hn\":\"Recommended as an approachable introduction to dependent types and a preview of what The Little Typer covers.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"intro\",\"primary_topic\":\"dependent types\",\"categories\":[\"Programming language design\",\"Logic & formal methods\",\"Functional programming\"],\"tags\":[\"dependent types\",\"type theory\",\"the little typer\",\"proofs\",\"idris\",\"pie\"],\"quote\":\"Here's an intro to dependent types from David Christiansen\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.0},{\"vid\":\"W6aKQ-eBFk0\",\"title\":\"AMD Ryzen Eco Mode Deep-Dive & Benchmarks on R9 7950X (Zen 4)\",\"channel\":\"Gamers Nexus\",\"summary\":\"Gamers Nexus benchmarks the Ryzen 9 7950X in its BIOS Eco Mode presets (65W, 105W and stock 170W). It measures the performance cost against the power and heat savings.\",\"why_hn\":\"Cited as evidence that Eco Mode gives large power savings for a small performance loss on Zen 4.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"cpu power efficiency\",\"categories\":[\"Computer architecture & CPUs\",\"Consumer devices & gadgets\"],\"tags\":[\"ryzen 7950x\",\"eco mode\",\"zen 4\",\"benchmarks\",\"power consumption\"],\"quote\":\"So just enable it and enjoy way more reasonable and efficient power usage with basically almost the same performance.\",\"recommenders\":3,\"score\":2.0},{\"vid\":\"WHj2GaPuEhY\",\"title\":\"Noam Chomsky: \\\"Free Markets?\\\"\",\"channel\":\"Santarchy\",\"summary\":\"A 1997 Noam Chomsky talk at Northeastern University about the gap between free-market rhetoric and practice. He argues that business relies heavily on state intervention, and he discusses trade, NAFTA and labour versus capital mobility.\",\"why_hn\":\"Linked repeatedly in threads on monopolies, protectionism, and subsidies, usually as a source for the argument that free markets are an ideology more than a reality.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"free markets and state intervention\",\"categories\":[\"Microeconomics & behavioral economics\",\"Free speech, censorship & civil liberties\",\"Macroeconomics & financial crises\"],\"tags\":[\"noam chomsky\",\"free markets\",\"capitalism\",\"nafta\",\"political economy\"],\"quote\":\"I highly recommend watching this talk by Noam Chomsky titled\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.0},{\"vid\":\"WITLR_qSPXk\",\"title\":\"Automation Dependency - Part One, by Capt. VanderBurgh (restored)\",\"channel\":\"flightcrewguide.com\",\"summary\":\"Part one of an American Airlines training video presented by Captain Warren VanderBurgh on automation dependency. It grew out of a program on wake turbulence avoidance, and this restored version has the audio cleaned up.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN cites it as the famous lecture on over-reliance on automation and on when to drop to a lower level of automation, applicable well beyond aviation.\",\"content_type\":\"lecture\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"automation dependency\",\"categories\":[\"Aviation & aerospace engineering\",\"Futurism & technology and society\"],\"tags\":[\"aviation\",\"automation\",\"human factors\",\"pilot training\",\"cockpit\"],\"quote\":\"a 1997 talk by an American Airlines trainer about automation dependency\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.0},{\"vid\":\"WMSBRk5WG58\",\"title\":\"Handmade Hero Day 021 - Loading Game Code Dynamically\",\"channel\":\"Molly Rocket\",\"summary\":\"Day 21 of Casey Muratori's Handmade Hero, which covers loading game code dynamically from a DLL on Windows. He builds hot reloading of C game code from scratch in about an hour and a half.\",\"why_hn\":\"Recommended as a clear, from-scratch demonstration of how simple code hot-reloading is with plain OS facilities.\",\"content_type\":\"tutorial\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"hot reloading game code\",\"categories\":[\"Game programming & engines\",\"C, C++, Rust, Go & systems languages\"],\"tags\":[\"handmade hero\",\"dll\",\"hot reload\",\"win32\",\"c programming\"],\"quote\":\"Casey Muratori writes a hot-reloading functionality for C from scratch in about an hour\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.0},{\"vid\":\"WNWYk4DdT_E\",\"title\":\"Giga Castings with Sandy | Evolution of Tesla Bodies In White\",\"channel\":\"Munro Live\",\"summary\":\"Sandy Munro and Cory discuss how Tesla Model 3 and Model Y bodies in white have evolved over five years, including giga castings and lean design.\",\"why_hn\":\"Cited as an expert's account of why gigacasting works and how Tesla manufacturing has changed.\",\"content_type\":\"interview\",\"level\":\"intermediate\",\"primary_topic\":\"tesla gigacasting manufacturing\",\"categories\":[\"Cars, EVs & motorcycles\",\"Manufacturing & industrial processes\"],\"tags\":[\"gigacasting\",\"sandy munro\",\"tesla\",\"body in white\",\"lean design\"],\"quote\":\"Sandy Munro is a leading expert in the auto industry, tears down all the vehicles and consults with all the major manufactures.\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.0},{\"vid\":\"WO2X3oZEJOA\",\"title\":\"Glitch Tokens - Computerphile\",\"channel\":\"Computerphile\",\"summary\":\"Rob Miles explains \\\"glitch\\\" tokens, odd strings in large language model vocabularies that make the model produce gibberish. He covers how they likely arise from tokenizer training data, such as Reddit usernames, that never appeared in the model's own training.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN points to it as the accessible explanation of why glitch tokens exist whenever tokenizers or odd GPT behavior come up.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"intro\",\"primary_topic\":\"llm tokenization\",\"categories\":[\"LLMs & generative AI\",\"Computer vision, speech & NLP\"],\"tags\":[\"glitch tokens\",\"tokenizers\",\"gpt\",\"ai safety\",\"bpe\"],\"quote\":\"it's also a good introduction to the topic.\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.0},{\"vid\":\"WU0gvPcc3jQ\",\"title\":\"The Matrix Awakens: An Unreal Engine 5 Experience\",\"channel\":\"Unreal Engine\",\"summary\":\"Epic's Unreal Engine 5 tech demo set in the Matrix universe, with Keanu Reeves and Carrie-Anne Moss. It moves from a cinematic to a playable car chase through a large detailed city, with a behind-the-scenes look at the rendering at the end.\",\"why_hn\":\"Cited as an impressive real-time rendering showcase, with Nanite and a huge photorealistic city, that rivals film CGI.\",\"content_type\":\"demo\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"real-time graphics\",\"categories\":[\"Computer graphics & rendering\",\"Game programming & engines\"],\"tags\":[\"unreal engine 5\",\"nanite\",\"the matrix\",\"real-time rendering\",\"tech demo\"],\"quote\":\"The fun part is t