ames\",\"summary\":\"A video essay arguing that the next major real-time strategy game will fail unless it gets the fundamentals right. It covers the playerbase and demographics, what older RTS games did well, and the roles of the engine, spectacle, development tools and player-generated content.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN recommends it for its argument that single-player campaigns and modding are overlooked in RTS design.\",\"content_type\":\"commentary\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"rts game design\",\"categories\":[\"Game design\",\"Gaming culture & analysis\",\"Indie game development\"],\"tags\":[\"rts\",\"modding\",\"single-player campaigns\",\"game industry\",\"player-generated content\"],\"quote\":\"makes a compelling case for why single-player campaign and mod-development experiences are often overlooked\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.0},{\"vid\":\"XgRlrBl-7Yg\",\"title\":\"The riddle of experience vs. memory | Daniel Kahneman\",\"channel\":\"TED\",\"summary\":\"In this TED talk, Nobel laureate Daniel Kahneman distinguishes the experiencing self from the remembering self, using examples such as vacations and colonoscopies. He explains how the two perceive happiness differently and what that means for economics, policy and self-awareness.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN commenters recommend it in threads on happiness and well-being as a clear account of why memory and experience of happiness diverge.\",\"content_type\":\"talk\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"happiness and memory\",\"categories\":[\"Psychology & human behavior\",\"Microeconomics & behavioral economics\"],\"tags\":[\"daniel kahneman\",\"behavioral economics\",\"experiencing self\",\"remembering self\",\"psychology\"],\"quote\":\"Daniel Khaneman talks about the experiencing self versus the remembering self\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.0},{\"vid\":\"XopSDJq6w8E\",\"title\":\"Are NEW Chinese buildings really FALLING DOWN?\",\"channel\":\"ADVChina\",\"summary\":\"The ADVChina hosts tour a villa neighborhood in southern China that was built only three years earlier and is already empty and deteriorating. They use it to discuss ghost cities, building quality and the real estate bubble.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN commenters cite it in threads on China's housing glut and construction quality as visual evidence of poor, empty new buildings.\",\"content_type\":\"documentary\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"china ghost cities\",\"categories\":[\"Macroeconomics & financial crises\",\"Civil engineering & construction\",\"Geopolitics & foreign policy\"],\"tags\":[\"china\",\"real estate\",\"ghost towns\",\"construction quality\",\"housing bubble\"],\"quote\":\"This video from last year was pretty eye opening to me.\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.0},{\"vid\":\"XwRSS7jeo5s\",\"title\":\"jacob collier tunes the piano\",\"channel\":\"George Collier\",\"summary\":\"A one-minute clip of Jacob Collier tuning a piano, remarking that it is not in tune at all. It touches on his views on equal temperament and tuning.\",\"why_hn\":\"Used as an example in music theory and tuning discussions of continuous-pitch thinking beyond equal temperament.\",\"content_type\":\"demo\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"tuning and temperament\",\"categories\":[\"Music theory, synthesis & production\",\"Music performance & songs\"],\"tags\":[\"jacob collier\",\"equal temperament\",\"piano tuning\",\"music theory\"],\"quote\":\"Jacob Collier has a good example of this[1] (I'm a huge fan).\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.0},{\"vid\":\"YHLU0Uej1WA\",\"title\":\"Ben Marking's Fake BBC Nuclear Attack Broadcast (Full Resolution, Uncut, Unedited)\",\"channel\":\"Tooth\",\"summary\":\"A 56-minute fake BBC nuclear attack news broadcast originally made by Ben Marking, re-uploaded in full resolution. It is a fictional breaking-news special depicting nuclear war, and the uploader states it is not real.\",\"why_hn\":\"Commenters bring it up in nuclear-fear and WWIII threads as an unnervingly realistic piece of fictional news coverage.\",\"content_type\":\"other\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"fictional nuclear war broadcast\",\"categories\":[\"Military history & warfare\",\"Documentaries & storytelling\",\"Film & TV clips\"],\"tags\":[\"nuclear war\",\"fake news broadcast\",\"bbc\",\"emergency alert\",\"fiction\"],\"quote\":\"I recommend waiting till nighttime and turning up the volume for extra effect.\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.0},{\"vid\":\"YJrOuBkYCMQ\",\"title\":\"Where The Real Chip Shortage Is\",\"channel\":\"Asianometry\",\"summary\":\"Asianometry explains that the worst of the 2021-22 chip shortage sits in trailing-edge semiconductors, not the leading-edge chips usually covered. It covers why those older-node fabs are so hard to expand and fix.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN commenters point to it as a clear explanation of why fabs aren't being built for older process nodes.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"semiconductor supply chain\",\"categories\":[\"Semiconductors & chip manufacturing\",\"Manufacturing & industrial processes\"],\"tags\":[\"chip shortage\",\"trailing-edge\",\"fabs\",\"semiconductors\",\"supply chain\"],\"quote\":\"This video seems to be doing much better job at explaining the problem\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.0},{\"vid\":\"YQ2QtKcK2dA\",\"title\":\"The Man behind Stable Diffusion\",\"channel\":\"Yannic Kilcher\",\"summary\":\"Yannic Kilcher interviews Emad Mostaque, founder of Stability AI, about the company's funding, its mission, and the release of Stable Diffusion. Topics include access to compute, handling harmful outputs, and avoiding the corrupting influence of profit.\",\"why_hn\":\"Commenters cite it during Stable Diffusion release debates as a source for Mostaque's vision and Stability's principles.\",\"content_type\":\"interview\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"stability ai and open generative models\",\"categories\":[\"LLMs & generative AI\",\"Tech