il)\",\"summary\":\"Marco Baringer's tutorial video on SLIME, the Emacs mode for developing Common Lisp. It demonstrates the interactive workflow of working against a live Lisp image.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN points to it to show what the Lisp REPL workflow is like and as a good tour of SLIME.\",\"content_type\":\"tutorial\",\"level\":\"intro\",\"primary_topic\":\"common lisp interactive development\",\"categories\":[\"Functional programming\",\"Testing, debugging & developer tools\"],\"tags\":[\"slime\",\"emacs\",\"common lisp\",\"repl\",\"swank\"],\"quote\":\"This is what the lisp repl is like. There's not much else like it\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.0},{\"vid\":\"_GVSLcqGP7g\",\"title\":\"Tomb Raider on the Nintendo Game Boy Advance is incredible | MVG\",\"channel\":\"Modern Vintage Gamer\",\"summary\":\"Modern Vintage Gamer looks at OpenLara, an open source Tomb Raider engine, running on the Game Boy Advance. The video explains how the port achieves playable speeds on the GBA's slow ARM CPU, with input from the developer XProger.\",\"why_hn\":\"HN points to it as coverage of an impressive 3D game port on very limited hardware.\",\"content_type\":\"explainer\",\"level\":\"general\",\"primary_topic\":\"game boy advance ports\",\"categories\":[\"Game history & retro gaming\",\"Game programming & engines\",\"Computer architecture & CPUs\"],\"tags\":[\"tomb raider\",\"openlara\",\"gba\",\"game ports\",\"retro hardware\"],\"quote\":\"I found some fascinating coverage of the OpenLara project, specifically for the port of Tomb Raider to the GBA.\",\"recommenders\":2,\"score\":2.0},{\"vid\":\"_NuvwndwYSY\",\"title\":\"Teletype Model 19 - Part 1: A Teletype Arrives for Restoration\",\"channel\":\"CuriousMarc\",\"summary\":\"CuriousMarc inspects a newly arrived Teletype Model 19, an early military unit built around a Model 15 keyboard and printer, after an initial rough cleaning. It is the first part of a restoration series and touches on 5-bit Baudot code.\",\"why_hn\":\"H